_id','7'),(74,23,'_menu_item_object','page'),(75,23,'_menu_item_target',''),(76,23,'_menu_item_classes','a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(77,23,'_menu_item_xfn',''),(78,23,'_menu_item_url',''),(79,24,'_menu_item_type','post_type'),(80,24,'_menu_item_menu_item_parent','0'),(81,24,'_menu_item_object_id','8'),(82,24,'_menu_item_object','page'),(83,24,'_menu_item_target',''),(84,24,'_menu_item_classes','a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(85,24,'_menu_item_xfn',''),(86,24,'_menu_item_url',''),(87,25,'_menu_item_type','post_type'),(88,25,'_menu_item_menu_item_parent','0'),(89,25,'_menu_item_object_id','10'),(90,25,'_menu_item_object','page'),(91,25,'_menu_item_target',''),(92,25,'_menu_item_classes','a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(93,25,'_menu_item_xfn',''),(94,25,'_menu_item_url',''),(108,39,'_ml_treatment_short','Clinical assessment and personalised plans for thinning, shedding and hair-fall concerns.'),(109,39,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Hair loss and thinning can follow stress, hormones, nutrition, medication or genetics. At Ma Lumière we first understand the pattern and the cause, then map a plan suited to your scalp and goals.</p>'),(110,39,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Assessment of the scalp and hair history, followed by targeted treatments and a maintenance routine designed around the underlying pattern of loss.</p>'),(111,39,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Men and women noticing increased shedding, widening parts, reduced density or a family history of thinning.</p>'),(112,39,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Diffuse hair fall, crown thinning, receding hairline, post-partum shedding, stress-related loss.</p>'),(113,39,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Progress is gradual — hair cycles take months. Your dermatologist sets realistic milestones at the consultation rather than promising fixed timelines.</p>'),(114,39,'_ml_treatment_process','Scalp and history assessment\nIdentifying contributing factors\nPersonalised in-clinic plan\nHome-care and maintenance routine'),(115,39,'_ml_treatment_sessions','4–6 (assessment-led)'),(116,39,'_ml_treatment_duration','45'),(117,39,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None'),(118,39,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Come with a note of recent illnesses, medications and any family history of thinning.</p>'),(119,39,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Follow the prescribed routine consistently; hair responds to sustained care, not one-off sessions.</p>'),(120,39,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is hair loss always permanent? || Not necessarily. Many forms are temporary or stabilisable once the trigger is identified — that is exactly what the consultation is for.\nWhen will I see change? || Hair grows slowly, so assessments are spaced over months to judge response fairly.'),(121,40,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-33756884.jpg'),(122,40,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Woman smiling and holding hair-care product bottles'),(123,40,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2400;s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"2026/09/pexels-33756884.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:306506;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-33756884-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9856;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-33756884-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:67933;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-33756884-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5490;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-33756884-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:82440;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-33756884-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:135829;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-33756884-1365x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1365;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:229941;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-33756884-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:134599;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-33756884-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:60660;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-33756884-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:97381;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-33756884-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:49219;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(124,39,'_thumbnail_id','98'),(125,41,'_ml_treatment_short','A calm, scheduled skin plan so you walk into your day with confidence — not last-minute fixes.'),(126,41,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Wedding skin is about timing. With a plan that starts early enough, concerns are addressed in a safe sequence — without risky last-minute experiments the week of the event.</p>'),(127,41,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>A staged plan combining in-clinic treatments and a simple home routine, sequenced so your skin is settled and glowing when it matters.</p>'),(128,41,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Brides, grooms and wedding parties planning ahead — ideally starting 8–12 weeks before the event.</p>'),(129,41,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Dullness, uneven tone, texture, breakouts, pre-event glow and overall skin confidence.</p>'),(130,41,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Expect steady improvement in clarity and radiance. Aggressive treatments are deliberately avoided close to your date.</p>'),(131,41,'_ml_treatment_process','Consultation and date-based timeline\nSkin analysis and priority setting\nStaged in-clinic treatments\nSimple home routine and check-ins'),(132,41,'_ml_treatment_sessions','Timeline-based (often 3–5)'),(133,41,'_ml_treatment_duration','40'),(134,41,'_ml_treatment_downtime','Minimal (treatment-dependent)'),(135,41,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Share your event date first — everything else is scheduled around it.</p>'),(136,41,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Keep new products out of the routine in the final weeks; introduce nothing untested before the day.</p>'),(137,41,'_ml_treatment_faqs','How early should I start? || About 2–3 months ahead gives comfortable room to stage treatments safely.\nCan I do something the week of the wedding? || Only gentle, low-risk care — anything more aggressive is scheduled well before your date.'),(138,42,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-3757942.jpg'),(139,42,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Woman relaxing at a spa in a white towel with flowers'),(140,42,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-3757942.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:102397;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3757942-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10849;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3757942-1024x683.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:683;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:59464;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3757942-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5534;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3757942-768x512.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:512;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:39211;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3757942-1536x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1536;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:106466;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3757942-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:90768;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3757942-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:44476;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3757942-900x1067.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:72652;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3757942-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:38200;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(141,41,'_thumbnail_id','99'),(142,43,'_ml_treatment_short','Evidence-led acne care and considered scar treatment — for active breakouts and their after-effects.'),(143,43,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Acne is common, but the reasons behind it vary — and so does the right treatment. We treat the active breakouts first, then address the marks and texture they leave behind.</p>'),(144,43,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Assessment of acne type and severity, medical management of active breakouts, then a staged approach to post-acne marks and texture once skin is stable.</p>'),(145,43,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone with active pimples, cysts or persistent congestion, or leftover red marks, pits or uneven texture after acne.</p>'),(146,43,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Whiteheads, blackheads, inflammatory breakouts, hormonal acne, post-acne redness, marks and textural scarring.</p>'),(147,43,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Active acne improves over weeks to months; scar treatment is planned only after skin is stable, and expectations are set per scar type.</p>'),(148,43,'_ml_treatment_process','Acne assessment and severity grading\nActive-breakout treatment plan\nHome routine and lifestyle review\nScar and texture phase once skin is clear'),(149,43,'_ml_treatment_sessions','Acne: ongoing; scars: 4–6'),(150,43,'_ml_treatment_duration','30'),(151,43,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–48 hours'),(152,43,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Bring a list of products and treatments you have already tried.</p>'),(153,43,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Do not pick or squeeze — it is the single biggest cause of avoidable scarring.</p>'),(154,43,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Should I treat acne or scars first? || Always the active acne. Scar treatments are planned once breakouts are controlled.\nIs acne treatment permanent? || It controls and clears active acne; maintenance depends on your pattern and triggers.'),(155,44,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-6475981.jpg'),(156,44,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of a young woman with acne'),(157,44,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2399;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-6475981.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:333229;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6475981-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9370;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6475981-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:68379;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6475981-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4846;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6475981-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:84877;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6475981-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:146192;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6475981-1366x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1366;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:252154;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6475981-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:127522;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6475981-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:52843;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6475981-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:100724;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6475981-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:43781;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(158,43,'_thumbnail_id','100'),(159,45,'_ml_treatment_short','Clinic-grade laser for long-term hair reduction across face and body, planned around your skin type.'),(160,45,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Laser hair reduction targets the follicle to progressively reduce regrowth. Settings are chosen for your skin tone and hair type — safety and response both depend on getting that match right.</p>'),(161,45,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Cooling-assisted laser energy is delivered over the treatment area to disable active follicles; regrowth becomes finer and lighter over successive sessions.</p>'),(162,45,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Most skin types and areas — face, underarms, arms, legs, bikini and back. A patch test is done before full courses.</p>'),(163,45,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Unwanted facial or body hair, ingrown hairs, irritation from shaving and waxing, repeated regrowth.</p>'),(164,45,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Progressive reduction in density and thickness. Maintenance may occasionally be needed, as hormones can stimulate new follicles over time.</p>'),(165,45,'_ml_treatment_process','Consultation and patch test\nArea mapping and settings selection\nSession delivery with cooling\nSpaced follow-up sessions'),(166,45,'_ml_treatment_sessions','6–8, spaced 4–8 weeks'),(167,45,'_ml_treatment_duration','20–60'),(168,45,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None'),(169,45,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>No waxing or plucking for 4 weeks before; avoid sun exposure to the area.</p>'),(170,45,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Expect mild redness for a short while — use SPF and skip hot showers, saunas and scrubs for 24–48 hours.</p>'),(171,45,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Does laser hair reduction hurt? || Most people describe a quick warm snap; cooling keeps it comfortable.\nHow many sessions will I need? || Typically 6–8, but skin type, area and hair colour all affect the count.'),(172,46,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-3985356.jpg'),(173,46,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Cosmetologist performing a laser treatment on a client in a clinic'),(174,46,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-3985356.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:121564;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3985356-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:11825;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3985356-1024x683.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:683;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:65406;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3985356-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5727;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3985356-768x512.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:512;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:42645;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3985356-1536x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1536;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:120480;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3985356-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:102278;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3985356-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:49140;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3985356-900x1067.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:70254;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3985356-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:38719;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:12:\"taras_chaban\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:12:\"taras_chaban\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(175,45,'_thumbnail_id','101'),(176,47,'_ml_treatment_short','Targeted care for dark spots, sun damage and uneven tone — built around your skin, not a trend.'),(177,47,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Pigmentation comes in many forms — sun spots, post-acne marks, melasma — and each responds differently. Correct diagnosis is the first step, because treating the wrong type can make it worse.</p>'),(178,47,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Diagnosis of the pigment type, a barrier-safe home routine, and staged in-clinic treatment to fade excess pigment evenly.</p>'),(179,47,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone with sun spots, post-inflammatory marks, melasma patches or a generally uneven complexion.</p>'),(180,47,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Sun spots, freckling, post-acne dark marks, melasma, dullness and blotchy tone.</p>'),(181,47,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Marks fade gradually over multiple cycles of treatment; daily SPF and avoiding triggers matter as much as the treatment itself.</p>'),(182,47,'_ml_treatment_process','Pigment diagnosis and skin analysis\nSun-protection and barrier plan\nStaged in-clinic treatment\nReview and maintenance'),(183,47,'_ml_treatment_sessions','4–6'),(184,47,'_ml_treatment_duration','30'),(185,47,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–several days (treatment-dependent)'),(186,47,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Stop any self-tanning products and share your current skincare with us at the consult.</p>'),(187,47,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Daily broad-spectrum SPF and sun avoidance are essential — pigment returns quickly without them.</p>'),(188,47,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is pigmentation permanent? || Many forms fade substantially; melasma in particular can relapse, so maintenance is planned.\nCan I treat it in summer? || Often yes with the right protocol and strict sun protection — we decide case by case.'),(189,48,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-6476079.jpg'),(190,48,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Woman applying facial cream with clear, even skin'),(191,48,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2399;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-6476079.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:383273;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476079-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10198;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476079-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:78600;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476079-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5150;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476079-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:97222;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6476079-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:166738;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6476079-1366x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1366;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:287400;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476079-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:147058;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476079-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:62701;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476079-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:114504;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476079-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:51733;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(192,47,'_thumbnail_id','102'),(193,49,'_ml_treatment_short','Q-switched laser treatment to fade unwanted tattoos, spaced safely across the clearing cycle.'),(194,49,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Laser tattoo removal breaks the ink into particles your body then clears. The process is gradual — and deliberately so — with sessions spaced to let the skin recover and the ink lift between rounds.</p>'),(195,49,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Short-pulse laser energy shatters ink particles in the skin, which are then removed naturally by the body over the following weeks.</p>'),(196,49,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Healthy adults seeking to fade or remove an unwanted tattoo of any age, size or colour (colour affects pace, not feasibility).</p>'),(197,49,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Unwanted tattoos, faded or regretted designs, partially removed artwork needing completion.</p>'),(198,49,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Progressive lightening; complete clearance varies with ink, depth and aftercare. Partial fading is also a common, useful goal.</p>'),(199,49,'_ml_treatment_process','Consultation and tattoo assessment\nPatch test where appropriate\nLaser session with cooling\nSpaced review as the ink clears'),(200,49,'_ml_treatment_sessions','6–10+ (design-dependent)'),(201,49,'_ml_treatment_duration','10–30'),(202,49,'_ml_treatment_downtime','3–7 days (surface)'),(203,49,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Avoid sun on the area; do not pick or scrub the skin before your session.</p>'),(204,49,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Keep the area clean, moisturised and out of the sun; blistered skin must not be picked.</p>'),(205,49,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Will it fully disappear? || Many tattoos clear significantly; some fade to a faint shadow — realistic expectations are set at consultation.\nWhy are sessions months apart? || Your body needs that time to flush the shattered ink — spacing is what makes it work.'),(206,50,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-32522497.jpg'),(207,50,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of detailed tattoo being inked on a forearm'),(208,50,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2400;s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"2026/09/pexels-32522497.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:568089;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-32522497-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:13231;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-32522497-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:100363;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-32522497-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:6608;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-32522497-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:125650;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-32522497-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:224382;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-32522497-1365x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1365;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:403740;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-32522497-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:195539;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-32522497-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:77737;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-32522497-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:149245;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-32522497-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:64017;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:6:\"Ferraz\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:6:\"Ferraz\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(209,49,'_thumbnail_id','103'),(210,51,'_ml_treatment_short','A long-view approach to skin health — resilience, texture and radiance at every age.'),(211,51,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Aging is not a problem to fix but a process to support. The aim is skin that stays healthy, comfortable and vibrant — with treatments chosen for how you actually want to look, not against your years.</p>'),(212,51,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>A combination of barrier-focused home care and in-clinic treatments that support collagen, tone and hydration over time.</p>'),(213,51,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone noticing dullness, fine lines, laxity, uneven texture or reduced resilience — starting at any age.</p>'),(214,51,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Fine lines, loss of firmness, uneven tone, dullness, dryness and texture changes.</p>'),(215,51,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Improvement is cumulative — skin looks progressively fresher and better supported rather than suddenly different.</p>'),(216,51,'_ml_treatment_process','Skin assessment and goals\nBarrier-first home routine\nStaged rejuvenation treatments\nOngoing review'),(217,51,'_ml_treatment_sessions','3–6 per cycle'),(218,51,'_ml_treatment_duration','45'),(219,51,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–48 hours'),(220,51,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Arrive without makeup where possible so we can assess your skin accurately.</p>'),(221,51,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Daily SPF and a simple, consistent routine outperform complicated rotating regimens.</p>'),(222,51,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is it only for older skin? || No — healthy-aging care is about prevention and maintenance as much as correction.\nHow soon will I notice? || Hydration and glow can show quickly; collagen-driven changes build over months.'),(223,52,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-10222448.jpg'),(224,52,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Older woman applying skincare to her face'),(225,52,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"2026/09/pexels-10222448.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:113031;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-10222448-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8177;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-10222448-1024x683.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:683;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:54047;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-10222448-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4970;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-10222448-768x512.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:512;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:33349;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-10222448-1536x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1536;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:109753;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-10222448-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:91827;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-10222448-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:41287;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-10222448-900x1067.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:93407;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-10222448-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:40732;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(226,51,'_thumbnail_id','104'),(227,53,'_ml_treatment_short','Subtle, anatomy-led injectable work — softening, balancing and contouring without looking done.'),(228,53,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Good injectable work is the kind nobody can point to — a rested face, balanced proportions, expressions that still move. Everything starts with a facial assessment, not a menu.</p>'),(229,53,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>A detailed facial assessment, followed by precisely planned placement of anti-wrinkle or volume treatments to balance and soften — never to freeze or overfill.</p>'),(230,53,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Adults seeking subtle refinement of expression lines, volume balance or facial proportion — after a full consultation.</p>'),(231,53,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Dynamic expression lines, mid-face volume loss, contour imbalance and tired-looking features.</p>'),(232,53,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Refined, natural-looking change. Longevity varies by treatment area and product, and is discussed honestly beforehand.</p>'),(233,53,'_ml_treatment_process','Facial assessment and mapping\nTreatment plan and consent\nPrecise in-clinic placement\nTwo-week review'),(234,53,'_ml_treatment_sessions','1 per cycle (reviewed)'),(235,53,'_ml_treatment_duration','30'),(236,53,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–48 hours'),(237,53,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Avoid alcohol, anti-inflammatories and blood thinners for 24–48 hours unless medically prescribed — confirm with us first.</p>'),(238,53,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Skip intense exercise, saunas and facial treatments for 24–48 hours; attend the review appointment.</p>'),(239,53,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Will I still look like myself? || That is the aim — the plan is built around your features, not a template.\nHow long does it last? || It depends on the product and area; we set expectations before you consent to anything.'),(240,54,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-6954117.jpg'),(241,54,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of a woman applying makeup to her face'),(242,54,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2400;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-6954117.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:204470;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6954117-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8022;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6954117-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:45151;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6954117-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4536;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6954117-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:54864;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6954117-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:93498;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6954117-1365x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1365;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:167688;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6954117-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:84356;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6954117-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:35788;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6954117-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:62117;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6954117-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:30392;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(243,53,'_thumbnail_id','105'),(244,55,'_ml_treatment_short','Texture-focused care to refine the look of enlarged pores and keep congestion under control.'),(245,55,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Pores cannot be permanently erased, but their appearance can be genuinely refined — with the right mix of clearing, texture work and consistent home care.</p>'),(246,55,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Decongestion, gentle resurfacing and a maintenance routine that keeps pores clear and skin texture smoother over time.</p>'),(247,55,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Oily or combination skin, visible pores on the nose, chin and cheeks, and skin with recurring congestion.</p>'),(248,55,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Visible pore size, blackheads, uneven surface texture and shine-related congestion.</p>'),(249,55,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Pores look smaller and skin feels smoother; the effect depends on consistent maintenance rather than a one-time fix.</p>'),(250,55,'_ml_treatment_process','Skin and congestion assessment\nIn-clinic clearing or resurfacing\nOil-balancing home routine\nPeriodic maintenance'),(251,55,'_ml_treatment_sessions','3–4'),(252,55,'_ml_treatment_duration','40'),(253,55,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–24 hours'),(254,55,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Arrive with clean skin; skip strong actives the night before if we have advised it.</p>'),(255,55,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Do not squeeze — it stretches the pore and pushes congestion deeper.</p>'),(256,55,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Can pores actually shrink? || They cannot permanently close, but congestion and texture changes make them look markedly smaller.\nIs it related to oily skin? || Often yes — oil and congestion are usually part of the same pattern we treat.'),(257,56,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-6476083.jpg'),(258,56,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of skin extraction tools used in dermatological treatment'),(259,56,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2400;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-6476083.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:592789;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476083-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:11428;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476083-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:115349;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476083-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5296;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476083-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:146064;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6476083-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:258317;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6476083-1365x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1365;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:441536;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476083-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:196888;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476083-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:82321;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6476083-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:165714;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6476083-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:68605;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(260,55,'_thumbnail_id','56'),(261,57,'_ml_treatment_short','Assessment-first removal of benign moles and skin tags, with the right method for each lesion.'),(262,57,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Moles and skin tags are common and usually benign — but nothing is removed without first checking that it is safe to do so. Assessment always comes before removal.</p>'),(263,57,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Examination and, where needed, confirmation of benign nature — followed by a removal method chosen for the lesion and its location.</p>'),(264,57,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Benign-appearing facial or body moles, raised moles and skin tags in areas of friction or irritation.</p>'),(265,57,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Facial moles, raised moles, skin tags on the neck, underarms or eyelids, and lesions that catch on clothing.</p>'),(266,57,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Lesion removed with minimal disruption; a small, faint mark may remain and is discussed before treatment.</p>'),(267,57,'_ml_treatment_process','Lesion examination\nSuitability and method discussion\nRemoval in clinic\nHealing review'),(268,57,'_ml_treatment_sessions','Usually 1'),(269,57,'_ml_treatment_duration','20'),(270,57,'_ml_treatment_downtime','A few days (site-dependent)'),(271,57,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Do not attempt to remove moles or tags at home — self-treatment risks infection and scarring.</p>'),(272,57,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Keep the site clean and protected; attend review if healing is slower than expected.</p>'),(273,57,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is every mole suitable for removal? || No — any lesion that is suspicious is assessed differently and may be referred for further evaluation.\nWill there be a scar? || A fine mark is possible; method and location determine how discreet it is.'),(274,58,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-31403887.jpg'),(275,58,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of a woman with smooth, clear skin'),(276,58,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2399;s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"2026/09/pexels-31403887.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:404080;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-31403887-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5537;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-31403887-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:58720;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-31403887-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:3045;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-31403887-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:76621;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-31403887-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:151749;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-31403887-1366x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1366;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:298099;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-31403887-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:148536;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-31403887-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:51207;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-31403887-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:94797;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-31403887-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:37435;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(277,57,'_thumbnail_id','58'),(278,59,'_ml_treatment_short','Practical treatment for sweating that goes beyond normal — underarms, palms and beyond.'),(279,59,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Excessive sweating is a medical concern, not a personal failing. When sweat disrupts work, clothing or confidence, it is worth treating — and it responds well to the right approach.</p>'),(280,59,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Assessment of the pattern and possible contributors, followed by area-specific treatment to reduce sweat output where it matters most.</p>'),(281,59,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone whose sweating soaks clothing, marks surfaces or limits daily activities despite normal hygiene.</p>'),(282,59,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Underarm sweating, sweaty palms and soles, social discomfort and clothing damage from perspiration.</p>'),(283,59,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Noticeable reduction in sweating in treated areas; duration of response depends on the method used.</p>'),(284,59,'_ml_treatment_process','Pattern assessment\nContributor review (medication, thyroid)\nArea-specific treatment plan\nFollow-up and adjustment'),(285,59,'_ml_treatment_sessions','Method-dependent (often 1–4)'),(286,59,'_ml_treatment_duration','30'),(287,59,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None'),(288,59,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Arrive with clean, product-free skin in the area to be treated.</p>'),(289,59,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Follow the area-specific aftercare provided; report any unusual reaction promptly.</p>'),(290,59,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is it just being \'hot\'? || No — hyperhidrosis is sweating beyond what the body needs, and it is a recognised treatable condition.\nCan it affect more than underarms? || Yes — palms, soles and face are common too; treatment is matched to the area.'),(291,60,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-9165659.jpg'),(292,60,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of a woman with water droplets on her skin'),(293,60,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2400;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-9165659.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:188162;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-9165659-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8181;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-9165659-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:52375;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-9165659-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4659;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-9165659-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:62933;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-9165659-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:100152;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-9165659-1365x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1365;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:160159;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-9165659-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:106554;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-9165659-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:50191;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-9165659-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:74742;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-9165659-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:39431;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:16:\"Dimenshtein Olga\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:16:\"Dimenshtein Olga\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(294,59,'_thumbnail_id','60'),(295,61,'_ml_treatment_short','Resurfacing and barrier-focused care for rough, bumpy or uneven surface texture.'),(296,61,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Texture shows up as roughness, small bumps or makeup that sits unevenly. It usually reflects a mix of dead-cell build-up, congestion and barrier state — all of which can be improved.</p>'),(297,61,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Gentle resurfacing paired with barrier repair, repeated at sensible intervals so skin becomes smoother without becoming sensitised.</p>'),(298,61,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Rough or bumpy skin, uneven makeup application, post-acne texture and general dullness of surface.</p>'),(299,61,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Roughness, small bumps, closed comedones, post-acne texture and a dull, lacklustre surface.</p>'),(300,61,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Skin feels softer and looks more even, building over several cycles of treatment and consistent home care.</p>'),(301,61,'_ml_treatment_process','Texture and barrier assessment\nGentle resurfacing treatment\nBarrier-supportive home care\nRepeat at spaced intervals'),(302,61,'_ml_treatment_sessions','3–4'),(303,61,'_ml_treatment_duration','40'),(304,61,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–48 hours'),(305,61,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Pause strong retinoids or acids a few days before, as advised at consultation.</p>'),(306,61,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Moisturise generously and wear SPF — resurfaced skin is more sun-sensitive.</p>'),(307,61,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Should I exfoliate more at home? || Usually less, not more — over-exfoliation is a common cause of the roughness people try to scrub away.\nHow long to feel a difference? || Most notice smoother feel within a few weeks of starting a paced plan.'),(308,62,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-3373716.jpg'),(309,62,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up portrait of a woman with smooth, healthy skin'),(310,62,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2397;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-3373716.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:328712;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373716-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8300;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373716-684x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:684;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:75694;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373716-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:3651;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373716-768x1151.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1151;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:93910;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3373716-1025x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1025;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:160916;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3373716-1367x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1367;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:265798;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373716-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:113573;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373716-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:49887;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373716-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:101190;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373716-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:42663;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(311,61,'_thumbnail_id','62'),(312,63,'_ml_treatment_short','Radiance-focused treatments for skin that looks flat, tired or lacking in light.'),(313,63,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Dull skin is usually a surface problem — slow cell turnover, dehydration and barrier wear rather than anything deeper. That makes it one of the more rewarding concerns to treat.</p>'),(314,63,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Hydration and gentle resurfacing to lift dull surface cells, supported by a barrier-first routine that keeps light in the skin.</p>'),(315,63,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Skin that looks flat or tired despite rest, with dehydration, roughness or a lack of glow.</p>'),(316,63,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Dullness, dehydration, sallow tone, tired-looking skin and loss of radiance.</p>'),(317,63,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Skin looks fresher and more luminous; hydration effects are quick, tone evenness builds over time.</p>'),(318,63,'_ml_treatment_process','Skin and hydration assessment\nGentle resurfacing or glow treatment\nBarrier-first home routine\nSeasonal review'),(319,63,'_ml_treatment_sessions','2–4'),(320,63,'_ml_treatment_duration','45'),(321,63,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None'),(322,63,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Hold off on strong actives the night before your appointment if advised.</p>'),(323,63,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Daily SPF keeps the glow from being undone by sun exposure.</p>'),(324,63,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is dullness a skin type? || No — it is usually a condition driven by surface build-up and dehydration, which is why it responds well to treatment.\nDo I need many sessions? || Often a short course is enough; maintenance keeps it going.'),(325,64,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-34775447.jpg'),(326,64,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Smiling woman with radiant, glowing skin'),(327,64,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:2399;s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"2026/09/pexels-34775447.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:319079;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-34775447-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:11204;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-34775447-683x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:683;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:76070;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-34775447-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5314;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-34775447-768x1152.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1152;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:93080;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-34775447-1024x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:153456;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"pexels-34775447-1366x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1366;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:251503;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-34775447-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:114512;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-34775447-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:51772;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-34775447-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:99510;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-34775447-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:45404;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:12:\"Farhad Irani\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:12:\"Farhad Irani\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(328,63,'_thumbnail_id','64'),(329,65,'_ml_treatment_short','Refresh tired, depleted skin with treatments that restore comfort, bounce and definition.'),(330,65,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Facial rejuvenation is about restoring — hydration, definition and comfort — rather than changing what makes your face yours. The plan is built from how your skin behaves now.</p>'),(331,65,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>A personalised combination of hydrating, resurfacing and firming treatments sequenced for steady, natural-looking renewal.</p>'),(332,65,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone feeling their skin looks tired, depleted or less defined and wanting a refreshed, natural result.</p>'),(333,65,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Fatigue, dehydration, loss of bounce, uneven tone and early textural change.</p>'),(334,65,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Skin looks rested and more resilient; results build across the planned sequence rather than overnight.</p>'),(335,65,'_ml_treatment_process','Consultation and skin assessment\nPersonalised treatment sequence\nSpaced in-clinic sessions\nHome care and review'),(336,65,'_ml_treatment_sessions','3–5'),(337,65,'_ml_treatment_duration','50'),(338,65,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None–48 hours'),(339,65,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Share any recent procedures or active prescriptions before we plan the sequence.</p>'),(340,65,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>Keep the routine simple and consistent while the sequence is in progress.</p>'),(341,65,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Is this the same as injectables? || Not necessarily — rejuvenation can be entirely skin-focused; injectables are a separate decision.\nWhen will it show? || Hydration responds quickly; firmness and texture build over the following weeks.'),(342,66,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-6874424.jpg'),(343,66,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Senior woman applying a hydrating facial sheet mask'),(344,66,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-6874424.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:112512;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6874424-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9430;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6874424-1024x683.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:683;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:56916;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6874424-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5011;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6874424-768x512.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:512;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:35963;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-6874424-1536x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1536;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:111365;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6874424-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:92693;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6874424-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:43089;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-6874424-900x1067.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1067;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:80488;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-6874424-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:640;s:6:\"height\";i:640;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:38686;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(345,65,'_thumbnail_id','66'),(346,67,'_ml_treatment_short','Simple, evidence-led routines and periodic checks — so small concerns stay small.'),(347,67,'_ml_treatment_intro','<p>Prevention is the least dramatic part of dermatology and the most effective. Daily sun protection, a barrier-respecting routine and periodic checks do more than any late-stage correction.</p>'),(348,67,'_ml_treatment_overview','<p>Personalised routine design focused on protection and barrier health, with periodic skin checks to catch changes early.</p>'),(349,67,'_ml_treatment_suitable','<p>Anyone wanting to protect good skin, starting early, or with sun exposure, family history or prior skin concerns.</p>'),(350,67,'_ml_treatment_concerns','<p>Early sun damage, first fine lines, barrier weakening, and peace of mind through regular checks.</p>'),(351,67,'_ml_treatment_results','<p>Fewer surprises later: steadier skin, slower cumulative damage and changes caught while they are still simple.</p>'),(352,67,'_ml_treatment_process','Skin assessment\nTailored minimal routine\nSun-protection plan\nPeriodic skin checks'),(353,67,'_ml_treatment_sessions','Annual / as needed'),(354,67,'_ml_treatment_duration','30'),(355,67,'_ml_treatment_downtime','None'),(356,67,'_ml_treatment_pre','<p>Bring the products you currently use so we can simplify rather than replace unnecessarily.</p>'),(357,67,'_ml_treatment_post','<p>SPF every day is the single highest-value habit in the whole plan.</p>'),(358,67,'_ml_treatment_faqs','Do I really need a dermatologist for prevention? || Not constantly — but periodic checks add value, especially with sun exposure or family history.\nHow many products should I use? || Usually fewer than you think: protect, cleanse, moisturise, treat only what needs treating.'),(359,68,'_wp_attached_file','2026/09/pexels-3373725.jpg'),(360,68,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Close-up of a cosmetic product tube on a pink background'),(361,68,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1600;s:6:\"height\";i:1600;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/09/pexels-3373725.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:126443;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373725-300x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:6431;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3373725-1024x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:62034;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373725-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:2501;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373725-768x768.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:768;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:34045;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"pexels-3373725-1536x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1536;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:138628;}s:7:\"ml-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373725-1400x900.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1400;s:6:\"height\";i:900;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:80823;}s:7:\"ml-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373725-800x600.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:800;s:6:\"height\";i:600;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:31024;}s:11:\"ml-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"pexels-3373725-900x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:61913;}s:9:\"ml-square\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"pexels-3373725-640x640.jpg\";s:5:\"width