INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (2,1,'2026-09-22 19:34:58','2026-09-22 19:34:58','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is an example page. It\'s different from a blog post because it will stay in one place and will show up in your site navigation (in most themes). Most people start with an About page that introduces them to potential site visitors. It might say something like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hi there! I\'m a bike messenger by day, aspiring actor by night, and this is my website. I live in Los Angeles, have a great dog named Jack, and I like pi&#241;a coladas. (And gettin\' caught in the rain.)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>...or something like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The XYZ Doohickey Company was founded in 1971, and has been providing quality doohickeys to the public ever since. Located in Gotham City, XYZ employs over 2,000 people and does all kinds of awesome things for the Gotham community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As a new WordPress user, you should go to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/wp-admin/\">your dashboard</a> to delete this page and create new pages for your content. Have fun!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Sample Page','','publish','closed','open','','sample-page','','','2026-09-22 19:34:58','2026-09-22 19:34:58','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/?page_id=2',0,'page','',0),(3,1,'2026-09-22 19:34:58','2026-09-22 19:34:58','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we are</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Our website address is: http://localhost/malumere.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Comments</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>When visitors leave comments on the site we collect the data shown in the comments form, and also the visitor&#8217;s IP address and browser user agent string to help spam detection.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An anonymized string created from your email address (also called a hash) may be provided to the Gravatar service to see if you are using it. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/. After approval of your comment, your profile picture is visible to the public in the context of your comment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you upload images to the website, you should avoid uploading images with embedded location data (EXIF GPS) included. Visitors to the website can download and extract any location data from images on the website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cookies</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment on our site you may opt-in to saving your name, email address and website in cookies. These are for your convenience so that you do not have to fill in your details again when you leave another comment. These cookies will last for one year.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you visit our login page, we will set a temporary cookie to determine if your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your browser.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you log in, we will also set up several cookies to save your login information and your screen display choices. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for a year. If you select &quot;Remember Me&quot;, your login will persist for two weeks. If you log out of your account, the login cookies will be removed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you edit or publish an article, an additional cookie will be saved in your browser. This cookie includes no personal data and simply indicates the post ID of the article you just edited. It expires after 1 day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Embedded content from other websites</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Articles on this site may include embedded content (e.g. videos, images, articles, etc.). Embedded content from other websites behaves in the exact same way as if the visitor has visited the other website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These websites may collect data about you, use cookies, embed additional third-party tracking, and monitor your interaction with that embedded content, including tracking your interaction with the embedded content if you have an account and are logged in to that website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we share your data with</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you request a password reset, your IP address will be included in the reset email.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How long we retain your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained indefinitely. This is so we can recognize and approve any follow-up comments automatically instead of holding them in a moderation queue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For users that register on our website (if any), we also store the personal information they provide in their user profile. All users can see, edit, or delete their personal information at any time (except they cannot change their username). Website administrators can also see and edit that information.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What rights you have over your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you have an account on this site, or have left comments, you can request to receive an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, including any data you have provided to us. You can also request that we erase any personal data we hold about you. This does not include any data we are obliged to keep for administrative, legal, or security purposes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where your data is sent</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Visitor comments may be checked through an automated spam detection service.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n','Privacy Policy','','draft','closed','open','','privacy-policy','','','2026-09-22 19:34:58','2026-09-22 19:34:58','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/?page_id=3',0,'page','',0),(4,0,'2026-09-22 19:35:02','2026-09-22 19:35:02','<!-- wp:page-list /-->','Navigation','','publish','closed','closed','','navigation','','','2026-09-22 19:35:02','2026-09-22 19:35:02','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/navigation/',0,'wp_navigation','',0),(6,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','Home','','publish','closed','closed','','home','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/home/',0,'page','',0),(7,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','About','','publish','closed','closed','','about','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/about/',0,'page','',0),(8,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','Treatments','','publish','closed','closed','','treatments','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatments/',0,'page','',0),(9,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','Book Consultation','','publish','closed','closed','','book-consultation','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/',0,'page','',0),(10,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','Contact','','publish','closed','closed','','contact','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/contact/',0,'page','',0),(11,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','FAQs','','publish','closed','closed','','faqs','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/faqs/',0,'page','',0),(12,0,'2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','','Blog','','publish','closed','closed','','blog','','','2026-09-22 20:09:33','2026-09-22 20:09:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/blog/',0,'page','',0),(13,9,'2026-09-22 20:11:59','2026-09-22 20:11:59','At Ma Lumière, dermatology is a conversation. We begin every journey by listening — then build a plan around your skin, your concerns and your goals. This journal will grow with clinic-approved guidance on skin health, treatments and care.\n\n[CLINIC JOURNAL CONTENT REQUIRED]','Welcome to Ma Lumière','A note on how we work at the clinic.','publish','open','open','','welcome-to-ma-lumiere','','','2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/welcome-to-ma-lumiere/',0,'post','',0),(15,0,'2026-09-22 20:12:00','2026-09-22 20:12:00','[REAL, CONSENT-APPROVED CASE REQUIRED — before/after images must be uploaded here and must not reveal patient identity.]','Acne treatment — case reference','','publish','closed','closed','','acne-treatment-case-reference','','','2026-09-22 20:12:00','2026-09-22 20:12:00','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/results/acne-treatment-case-reference/',0,'ml_before_after','',0),(16,0,'2026-09-22 20:12:00','2026-09-22 20:12:00','Online booking is now open — choose a treatment, pick a date and time, and confirm your consultation in a few steps. You can still call or WhatsApp the clinic; contact details are on this page and in the footer.','How do I book an appointment?','','publish','closed','closed','','how-do-i-book-an-appointment','','','2026-11-21 02:54:32','2026-11-21 02:54:32','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/faq/how-do-i-book-an-appointment/',0,'ml_faq','',0),(17,0,'2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','17','','','2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-28 19:49:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/17/',2,'nav_menu_item','',0),(18,0,'2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','18','','','2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-28 19:49:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/18/',3,'nav_menu_item','',0),(20,0,'2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','20','','','2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-28 19:49:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/20/',6,'nav_menu_item','',0),(21,0,'2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','21','','','2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-28 19:49:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/21/',7,'nav_menu_item','',0),(22,0,'2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','22','','','2026-09-28 19:49:33','2026-09-28 19:49:33','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/22/',1,'nav_menu_item','',0),(23,0,'2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','23','','','2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/23/',0,'nav_menu_item','',0),(24,0,'2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','24','','','2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/24/',2,'nav_menu_item','',0),(25,0,'2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','25','','','2026-09-22 20:12:35','2026-09-22 20:12:35','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/09/22/25/',3,'nav_menu_item','',0),(39,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:17','2026-09-23 14:40:17','<p>Not every strand of hair fall is the same — some shed diffuse, some thin at the crown, some recede at the temples. A consultation helps identify what you are actually dealing with so the plan, not a generic product, does the work.</p><p>Every recommendation is made in-clinic after an examination; nothing here replaces a personal consultation.</p>','Hair Loss &amp; Hair Thinning','Clinical assessment and personalised plans for thinning, shedding and hair-fall concerns.','publish','closed','closed','','hair-loss-hair-thinning','','','2026-09-23 14:40:17','2026-09-23 14:40:17','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/hair-loss-hair-thinning/',1,'ml_treatment','',0),(40,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:18','2026-09-23 14:40:18','Woman smiling and holding hair-care product bottles','pexels-33756884','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-33756884','','','2026-09-23 14:40:18','2026-09-23 14:40:18','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-33756884/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(41,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:18','2026-09-23 14:40:18','<p>We work backwards from your date: what can be done, what should wait, and what must not be attempted close to the day. The goal is clear, comfortable, camera-ready skin — and no surprises.</p>','Pre-Wedding Skin Preparation','A calm, scheduled skin plan so you walk into your day with confidence — not last-minute fixes.','publish','closed','closed','','pre-wedding-skin-preparation','','','2026-09-23 14:40:18','2026-09-23 14:40:18','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pre-wedding-skin-preparation/',2,'ml_treatment','',0),(42,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:19','2026-09-23 14:40:19','Woman relaxing at a spa in a white towel with flowers','pexels-3757942','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-3757942','','','2026-09-23 14:40:19','2026-09-23 14:40:19','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-3757942/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(43,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:19','2026-09-23 14:40:19','<p>Active acne and acne scars are two different problems that need two different plans. Treating scars while skin is still breaking out wastes time; clearing breakouts without addressing texture leaves the reminder behind. We do both, in order.</p>','Acne &amp; Acne Scars','Evidence-led acne care and considered scar treatment — for active breakouts and their after-effects.','publish','closed','closed','','acne-acne-scars','','','2026-09-23 14:40:19','2026-09-23 14:40:19','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/acne-acne-scars/',3,'ml_treatment','',0),(44,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:20','2026-09-23 14:40:20','Close-up of a young woman with acne','pexels-6475981','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-6475981','','','2026-09-23 14:40:20','2026-09-23 14:40:20','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-6475981/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(45,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:20','2026-09-23 14:40:20','<p>Hair grows in cycles, and the laser only works on follicles in the active phase — which is why sessions are spaced several weeks apart. Consistency across the full cycle is what delivers the reduction.</p>','Laser Hair Reduction','Clinic-grade laser for long-term hair reduction across face and body, planned around your skin type.','publish','closed','closed','','laser-hair-reduction','','','2026-09-23 14:40:20','2026-09-23 14:40:20','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/',4,'ml_treatment','',0),(46,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:21','2026-09-23 14:40:21','Cosmetologist performing a laser treatment on a client in a clinic','pexels-3985356','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-3985356','','','2026-09-23 14:40:21','2026-09-23 14:40:21','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-3985356/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(47,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:21','2026-09-23 14:40:21','<p>Uneven tone is usually a mix of causes layered together. We identify which are active (especially sun and heat exposure) and which are settled marks, then treat accordingly — with sun protection as the non-negotiable foundation.</p>','Pigmentation &amp; Uneven Skin Tone','Targeted care for dark spots, sun damage and uneven tone — built around your skin, not a trend.','publish','closed','closed','','pigmentation-uneven-skin-tone','','','2026-09-23 14:40:21','2026-09-23 14:40:21','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pigmentation-uneven-skin-tone/',5,'ml_treatment','',0),(48,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:22','2026-09-23 14:40:22','Woman applying facial cream with clear, even skin','pexels-6476079','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-6476079','','','2026-09-23 14:40:22','2026-09-23 14:40:22','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-6476079/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(49,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:22','2026-09-23 14:40:22','<p>Colour, depth, ink density and location all change how a tattoo responds. Black ink usually clears fastest; multi-colour designs are treated in passes. We assess all of this before quoting a session range.</p>','Laser Tattoo Removal','Q-switched laser treatment to fade unwanted tattoos, spaced safely across the clearing cycle.','publish','closed','closed','','laser-tattoo-removal','','','2026-09-23 14:40:22','2026-09-23 14:40:22','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-tattoo-removal/',6,'ml_treatment','',0),(50,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:23','2026-09-23 14:40:23','Close-up of detailed tattoo being inked on a forearm','pexels-32522497','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-32522497','','','2026-09-23 14:40:23','2026-09-23 14:40:23','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-32522497/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(51,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:23','2026-09-23 14:40:23','<p>Collagen slows, the barrier thins, pigment and texture shift. Good rejuvenation respects all of it: protecting what works, restoring what has faded, and never pushing for an expression that is not yours.</p>','Healthy Aging &amp; Skin Rejuvenation','A long-view approach to skin health — resilience, texture and radiance at every age.','publish','closed','closed','','healthy-aging-skin-rejuvenation','','','2026-09-23 14:40:23','2026-09-23 14:40:23','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/healthy-aging-skin-rejuvenation/',7,'ml_treatment','',0),(52,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:24','2026-09-23 14:40:24','Older woman applying skincare to her face','pexels-10222448','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-10222448','','','2026-09-23 14:40:24','2026-09-23 14:40:24','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-10222448/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(53,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:24','2026-09-23 14:40:24','<p>Volume shifts and expression lines are mapped before anything is planned. The intent is refinement: softer lines, better balance, proportions that suit your face — with restraint built into the approach.</p>','Injectables &amp; Facial Contouring','Subtle, anatomy-led injectable work — softening, balancing and contouring without looking done.','publish','closed','closed','','injectables-facial-contouring','','','2026-09-23 14:40:24','2026-09-23 14:40:24','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/injectables-facial-contouring/',8,'ml_treatment','',0),(54,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:25','2026-09-23 14:40:25','Close-up of a woman applying makeup to her face','pexels-6954117','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-6954117','','','2026-09-23 14:40:25','2026-09-23 14:40:25','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-6954117/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(55,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:25','2026-09-23 14:40:25','<p>Pores look larger when they are congested, when oil production is high, and when surrounding skin loses firmness. We address each of those rather than chasing an impossible \"shrinking\" claim.</p>','Enlarged Pores','Texture-focused care to refine the look of enlarged pores and keep congestion under control.','publish','closed','closed','','enlarged-pores','','','2026-09-23 14:40:25','2026-09-23 14:40:25','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/enlarged-pores/',9,'ml_treatment','',0),(56,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:26','2026-09-23 14:40:26','Close-up of skin extraction tools used in dermatological treatment','pexels-6476083','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-6476083','','','2026-09-23 14:40:26','2026-09-23 14:40:26','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-6476083/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(57,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:26','2026-09-23 14:40:26','<p>Lesions on the face, neck, underarms or friction points are often both a cosmetic and a comfort concern. Method depends on the type, depth and location of the lesion, and on how discreet the resulting mark should be.</p>','Mole and Skin Tag Removal','Assessment-first removal of benign moles and skin tags, with the right method for each lesion.','publish','closed','closed','','mole-and-skin-tag-removal','','','2026-09-23 14:40:26','2026-09-23 14:40:26','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/mole-and-skin-tag-removal/',10,'ml_treatment','',0),(58,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:27','2026-09-23 14:40:27','Close-up of a woman with smooth, clear skin','pexels-31403887','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-31403887','','','2026-09-23 14:40:27','2026-09-23 14:40:27','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-31403887/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(59,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:27','2026-09-23 14:40:27','<p>Underarms, palms, soles and the face are the most common areas. We first rule out contributors like medication or thyroid issues, then choose treatment for the specific area — from topical options to in-clinic procedures.</p>','Hyperhidrosis (Excessive Sweating)','Practical treatment for sweating that goes beyond normal — underarms, palms and beyond.','publish','closed','closed','','hyperhidrosis-excessive-sweating','','','2026-09-23 14:40:27','2026-09-23 14:40:27','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/hyperhidrosis-excessive-sweating/',11,'ml_treatment','',0),(60,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','Close-up of a woman with water droplets on her skin','pexels-9165659','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-9165659','','','2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-9165659/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(61,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','<p>Smoothing skin is less about aggressive exfoliation and more about steady, barrier-respecting resurfacing. Overdoing it usually makes texture worse, so the plan is deliberately paced.</p>','Uneven Skin Texture','Resurfacing and barrier-focused care for rough, bumpy or uneven surface texture.','publish','closed','closed','','uneven-skin-texture','','','2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/uneven-skin-texture/',12,'ml_treatment','',0),(62,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','Close-up portrait of a woman with smooth, healthy skin','pexels-3373716','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-3373716','','','2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-3373716/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(63,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','<p>Think of it as restoring light: clearing the surface, replenishing hydration and protecting the barrier so skin reflects evenly again. Sleep, water and stress matter too — we address the whole picture.</p>','Dull &amp; Tired Skin','Radiance-focused treatments for skin that looks flat, tired or lacking in light.','publish','closed','closed','','dull-tired-skin','','','2026-09-23 14:40:28','2026-09-23 14:40:28','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/dull-tired-skin/',13,'ml_treatment','',0),(64,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:29','2026-09-23 14:40:29','Smiling woman with radiant, glowing skin','pexels-34775447','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-34775447','','','2026-09-23 14:40:29','2026-09-23 14:40:29','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-34775447/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(65,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:29','2026-09-23 14:40:29','<p>Combining hydration, texture and tone work in a considered sequence gives skin a genuine refresh without pushing toward an artificial look. Everything is spaced so recovery stays comfortable.</p>','Facial Rejuvenation','Refresh tired, depleted skin with treatments that restore comfort, bounce and definition.','publish','closed','closed','','facial-rejuvenation','','','2026-09-23 14:40:29','2026-09-23 14:40:29','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/facial-rejuvenation/',14,'ml_treatment','',0),(66,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:30','2026-09-23 14:40:30','Senior woman applying a hydrating facial sheet mask','pexels-6874424','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-6874424','','','2026-09-23 14:40:30','2026-09-23 14:40:30','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-6874424/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(67,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:30','2026-09-23 14:40:30','<p>There is no secret product — just a short routine you actually keep up, built around protection and a calm barrier, plus professional checks when something changes.</p>','Preventive Skin Care','Simple, evidence-led routines and periodic checks — so small concerns stay small.','publish','closed','closed','','preventive-skin-care','','','2026-09-23 14:40:30','2026-09-23 14:40:30','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/treatment/preventive-skin-care/',15,'ml_treatment','',0),(68,0,'2026-09-23 14:40:31','2026-09-23 14:40:31','Close-up of a cosmetic product tube on a pink background','pexels-3373725','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-3373725','','','2026-09-23 14:40:31','2026-09-23 14:40:31','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-3373725/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(69,0,'2026-09-23 14:44:36','2026-09-23 14:44:36','Welcome to Ma Lumière','pexels-34220329','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-34220329','','','2026-09-23 14:44:36','2026-09-23 14:44:36','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-34220329/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(70,0,'2026-09-23 16:08:57','2026-09-23 16:08:57','Glowing portrait of a woman in warm sunlight','pexels-33450622','','inherit','open','closed','','pexels-33450622','','','2026-09-23 16:08:57','2026-09-23 16:08:57','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/pexels-33450622/',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(72,1,'2026-09-28 19:50:09','2026-09-28 19:50:09','{\"version\": 3, \"isGlobalStylesUserThemeJSON\": true }','Custom Styles','','publish','closed','closed','','wp-global-styles-ma-lumiere','','','2026-09-28 19:50:09','2026-09-28 19:50:09','',0,'https://ma-lumiere.in/2026/09/28/wp-global-styles-ma-lumiere/',0,'wp_global_styles','',0),(73,1,'2026-09-28 19:51:12','2026-09-28 19:51:12','','About','','inherit','closed','closed','','7-autosave-v1','','','2026-09-28 19:51:12','2026-09-28 19:51:12','',7,'https://ma-lumiere.in/?p=73',0,'revision','',0),(75,9,'2026-10-20 09:30:00','2026-10-20 09:30:00','<p>If you are tired of shaving, waxing, or threading on repeat, laser hair reduction can offer a longer-term answer. But the results depend on more than the machine: your skin and hair type, the clinic\'s assessment, the treatment plan, and how you care for your skin between sessions.</p>\n\n<p>This guide explains what a course of laser hair reduction at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East looks like, so you can arrive at your consultation with realistic expectations.</p>\n\n<h2>What is laser hair reduction?</h2>\n<p>Laser hair reduction uses concentrated light to target pigment in the hair follicle. The heat damages follicles that are in an active growth phase, which can reduce hair growth over a course of sessions. It is called <strong>reduction</strong> rather than permanent removal because hair growth cycles, hormones, and individual biology all affect how much hair returns.</p>\n<p>It can be used on the face, underarms, arms, legs, bikini line, back, and chest. Unlike waxing, it does not pull hair from the root; unlike shaving, it works below the skin\'s surface.</p>\n\n<h2>Is laser hair reduction right for you?</h2>\n<p>Laser works best on hair with plenty of pigment. Dark hair on light-to-medium skin is the classic combination, but modern devices and adjusted settings can treat a wider range of skin tones. Grey, white, and very light blonde hair usually responds poorly because there is little pigment for the laser to target.</p>\n<p>Your consultation will consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your skin tone, hair colour, and hair thickness.</li>\n<li>Hormonal factors such as PCOS, thyroid conditions, or sudden changes in hair growth.</li>\n<li>Medications and supplements that can increase light sensitivity.</li>\n<li>Pregnancy, active skin infections, recent sun exposure, or a history of keloid scarring.</li>\n<li>Previous waxing, threading, laser, or electrolysis.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If laser is not the right choice for you, we will say so and discuss alternatives.</p>\n\n<h2>Your consultation at Ma Lumière</h2>\n<p>The consultation is a medical assessment, not a quick sales conversation. We review your history, examine the treatment area, and discuss what you want to change. A patch test may be performed to see how your skin responds before a full session.</p>\n<p>You will leave with a clear plan: the areas to treat, an estimated number of sessions, spacing, aftercare, and the cost. If you are unsure what to expect from a first appointment, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens during a session</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Skin preparation.</strong> The area is cleaned and make-up or lotion is removed. We may shave the area if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Eye protection.</strong> You and the clinician wear protective eyewear.</li>\n<li><strong>Cooling and comfort.</strong> Cold air or a cooling gel helps protect the skin. Most people describe the pulses as a quick rubber-band snap.</li>\n<li><strong>Treatment.</strong> The clinician moves the handpiece over the area, adjusting settings to your skin and comfort. Most areas take between 20 and 60 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>After the session.</strong> Mild redness or small bumps are common and usually settle within a few hours.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>How many sessions will you need?</h2>\n<p>Hair grows in cycles, and only hair in the active growth phase responds to laser. That is why a single session is not enough. A typical plan is <strong>6 to 8 sessions, spaced 4 to 8 weeks apart</strong>, depending on the area and your hair growth.</p>\n<p>Hormonal areas such as the face, chin, and neck may need more sessions or occasional maintenance. Your plan will be reviewed as your hair growth changes.</p>\n<p>Between sessions, shaving is fine. Waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating are not, because they remove the hair root that the next session needs to target.</p>\n\n<h2>Aftercare that protects your results</h2>\n<p>For the first 24 to 48 hours, keep the area calm. Use a gentle cleanser and moisturiser, avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise if you tend to flush, and apply sunscreen every day. Pause retinoids, exfoliating acids, and scrubs until your clinician confirms it is safe to restart.</p>\n<p>Sun protection matters between sessions, especially on the face. If you are planning a holiday or extended sun exposure, tell us before booking so we can adjust the schedule.</p>\n<p>For a fuller aftercare plan, read our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/06/post-treatment-skincare-recovery-guide/\">7-day post-treatment skincare guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you develop blistering, severe pain, spreading redness, fever, or signs of infection. These are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly.</p>\n\n<h2>Why choose Ma Lumière in Mira Road East?</h2>\n<p>Laser results depend on assessment, settings, consistency, and aftercare. At Ma Lumière, treatments are planned and supervised with a medical approach, and we will tell you honestly if a different option is a better fit. Our clinic is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East.</p>\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction treatment</a>, browse the full <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Does laser hair reduction hurt?</h3>\n<p>Most people feel a quick snapping or warming sensation. Comfort depends on the area, your sensitivity, and the settings used. Cooling and adjusted settings help.</p>\n<h3>Can I shave between sessions?</h3>\n<p>Yes, shaving is usually allowed. Avoid waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating between sessions.</p>\n<h3>Is laser safe for darker skin?</h3>\n<p>It can be, but the device, settings, and clinician\'s experience matter. A consultation and patch test help determine whether treatment is appropriate for your skin.</p>\n<h3>How long do results last?</h3>\n<p>Many people enjoy long-lasting reduction, but hair can return over time, especially with hormonal changes. Maintenance sessions may help.</p>\n<h3>Can I have laser hair reduction in summer?</h3>\n<p>Yes, with careful sun protection and scheduling around sun exposure. Tell us about holidays, beach days, or prolonged outdoor time before treatment.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Suitability and results vary; a consultation is required to plan treatment for your skin and medical history.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Laser Hair Reduction in Mira Road: A Session-by-Session Guide','A clear, session-by-session guide to laser hair reduction in Mira Road East — candidacy, comfort, aftercare, and how many sessions you may need.','publish','closed','closed','','laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide','','','2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/',0,'post','',0),(76,9,'2026-10-13 11:00:00','2026-10-13 11:00:00','<p>A skin consultation is where good treatment begins. It is not a sales pitch or a five-minute formality; it is the appointment where we work out what is happening in your skin, what you want to change, and which options are realistic for you.</p>\n<p>If you are booking your first appointment at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East, this guide explains what to expect and how to get the most from the conversation.</p>\n\n<h2>Why a consultation matters</h2>\n<p>Two people can have the same concern — acne, pigmentation, dullness, or hair thinning — for very different reasons. A treatment that suits one person may irritate another. The consultation connects the visible concern with your skin type, barrier health, medical history, lifestyle, and goals.</p>\n<p>It also gives you time to ask questions before committing to a plan. You should never feel rushed into a treatment.</p>\n\n<h2>What to bring</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Your current skincare.</strong> A list or photos of the products you use, including cleansers, actives, moisturisers, and sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Medications and supplements.</strong> Include prescription medicines, antibiotics, isotretinoin, hormonal treatments, and anything that can affect light sensitivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Allergies and past reactions.</strong> Tell us about reactions to products, lasers, peels, or anaesthetics.</li>\n<li><strong>Previous treatments.</strong> Dates and outcomes of facials, laser, peels, injectables, or dermatology treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos.</strong> If a concern comes and goes, bring photos of flare-ups.</li>\n<li><strong>Your goals and timeline.</strong> An event, a wedding, a holiday, or a gradual plan all change the approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Your questions.</strong> Write them down; it is easy to forget in the moment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What we assess</h2>\n<p>Every consultation starts with a conversation and a careful look at your skin. Depending on your concern, we may assess:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skin type, hydration, and barrier function.</li>\n<li>Acne, congestion, scarring, and pore size.</li>\n<li>Pigmentation, sun damage, and uneven tone.</li>\n<li>Texture, fine lines, and laxity.</li>\n<li>Hair growth, thinning, and scalp health.</li>\n<li>Lifestyle, sleep, stress, diet, and sun exposure.</li>\n<li>Medical and hormonal history that may affect the plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We will explain what we see in plain language and tell you whether the concern is best treated in clinic, at home, or with a combination of both.</p>\n\n<h2>How your treatment plan is built</h2>\n<p>A plan is more than a list of sessions. We consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>What matters most to you.</strong> Clearing acne, softening scarring, reducing hair, or improving glow are different goals.</li>\n<li><strong>What is realistic.</strong> Some concerns improve gradually; others need a staged approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Downtime.</strong> Work, events, and travel affect what we recommend.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance.</strong> Some treatments need follow-up to keep results.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget and pace.</strong> A plan should be sustainable, not a sprint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You will receive clear guidance on what to expect, how many sessions are estimated, what aftercare is needed, and what alternatives exist. If you are planning a wedding or a big event, our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pre-wedding-skin-preparation/\">pre-wedding skin preparation</a> page explains how we build a timeline around a date.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions worth asking</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What is causing my concern, and what would you rule out?</li>\n<li>What are my treatment options, including doing nothing for now?</li>\n<li>How many sessions might I need, and how will we review progress?</li>\n<li>What are the risks, side effects, and downtime?</li>\n<li>What should I pause or change in my routine before and after?</li>\n<li>What is the total cost, including follow-ups?</li>\n<li>What should I do if I do not see the result we expected?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is no such thing as a silly question. A good plan should make sense to you.</p>\n\n<h2>How to prepare</h2>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible, without heavy make-up, so we can assess it properly. Follow any instructions we send before your appointment. Do not start a new active ingredient or try a new facial right before the consultation; we want to see your skin as it normally behaves.</p>\n<p>If you are booking for laser hair reduction, avoid waxing or threading the area for a few weeks before your patch test. If you are booking for a skin concern, bring a list of products rather than the bottles.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens after the consultation</h2>\n<p>You will leave with a clear plan and next step. If a patch test is needed, we will arrange it. If you are ready to book, we will help you choose dates that fit your schedule and any events. If you want to think about it, that is fine too.</p>\n<p>Your plan can change. Skin changes, seasons change, and priorities change. We review progress as we go rather than locking you into a fixed package.</p>\n\n<h2>When to see a doctor sooner</h2>\n<p>Some concerns need prompt medical assessment rather than cosmetic treatment. Book sooner if you notice a new or changing mole, a sore that does not heal, bleeding, rapid hair loss, severe acne with pain or fever, or a rash that is spreading. These are not routine aesthetic concerns, and we will guide you to the right care.</p>\n\n<h2>Ready to book?</h2>\n<p>If you are looking for a <strong>skin consultation in Mira Road</strong>, Ma Lumière is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East. <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book your consultation</a>, explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or browse the <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/blog/\">skin journal</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How long does a consultation take?</h3>\n<p>Allow around 30 to 45 minutes, depending on your concern and the number of questions you have. A patch test may add a little time.</p>\n<h3>Do I need to prepare my skin?</h3>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible and bring a list of your current products. Follow any specific instructions sent before your appointment.</p>\n<h3>Will I be pressured to book a treatment?</h3>\n<p>No. The consultation is for assessment and planning. You can take time to decide.</p>\n<h3>Can I bring someone with me?</h3>\n<p>Yes, if it makes you more comfortable. Let us know in advance if you need extra time or support.</p>\n<h3>Can I book a consultation if I am not sure what treatment I need?</h3>\n<p>Yes. The consultation is designed to narrow down the options. You do not need to choose a treatment before you arrive.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. A consultation is required to assess your skin and recommend treatment.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','First Skin Consultation in Mira Road: What to Expect','What to bring, what we assess, and how your treatment plan is built at your first skin consultation in Mira Road East — plus questions worth asking.','publish','closed','closed','','first-skin-consultation-mira-road','','','2026-10-23 11:35:03','2026-10-23 11:35:03','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/',0,'post','',0),(77,9,'2026-10-06 10:15:00','2026-10-06 10:15:00','<p>The treatment is only part of the result. After a laser, facial, or skin treatment, your skin is temporarily more sensitive, and the right aftercare helps protect your results while reducing irritation.</p>\n<p>This guide covers the first week after treatment. Always follow the specific instructions given by your clinician, because aftercare depends on the treatment, your skin, and your medical history.</p>\n\n<h2>The first 24 hours</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Cleanse with a gentle, fragrance-free cleanser and lukewarm water. Avoid scrubbing.</li>\n<li>Apply a simple moisturiser and sunscreen. Skip make-up if your clinician advises it.</li>\n<li>Avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise that makes you flush.</li>\n<li>Do not use retinoids, exfoliating acids, scrubs, or strong active ingredients.</li>\n<li>Do not pick, scratch, or massage the treated area unless instructed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mild redness, warmth, or slight swelling can be normal. It should settle over hours to a couple of days.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 2 and 3</h2>\n<p>Keep the routine boring. Gentle cleanse, moisturise, and sunscreen. If your skin feels tight or dry, layer a hydrating serum under the moisturiser. Avoid exfoliation, waxing, threading, and hair removal creams on treated areas.</p>\n<p>If you had <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>, you may notice small bumps around the follicles. They usually settle. Do not scrub them. Shaving is generally fine unless your clinician has said otherwise.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 4 to 7</h2>\n<p>As redness settles, you can begin to return to your normal routine. Reintroduce one active ingredient at a time, every few days, rather than restarting everything at once. If your skin stings, flakes, or becomes red, stop and go back to the simple routine.</p>\n<p>Keep using sunscreen daily. Good sun protection is especially important after treatments for pigmentation, acne scarring, and facial rejuvenation.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients to pause</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Retinoids such as retinol, tretinoin, and adapalene.</li>\n<li>Exfoliating acids such as glycolic, salicylic, lactic, and mandelic acid.</li>\n<li>Physical scrubs, cleansing brushes, and at-home peeling devices.</li>\n<li>High-strength vitamin C, benzoyl peroxide, and alcohol-based toners if they sting.</li>\n<li>Fragrance-heavy products and essential oils on treated areas.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ask us when to restart each product. The timing depends on the treatment and how your skin is healing.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients that help</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ceramides</strong> to support the skin barrier.</li>\n<li><strong>Hyaluronic acid and glycerin</strong> for hydration.</li>\n<li><strong>Niacinamide</strong> if your skin tolerates it.</li>\n<li><strong>Panthenol and squalane</strong> for comfort.</li>\n<li><strong>Broad-spectrum sunscreen</strong> every morning.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do not need a ten-step routine. A gentle cleanser, a barrier-supporting moisturiser, and sunscreen are enough for most people in the first week.</p>\n\n<h2>Sun protection after treatment</h2>\n<p>Use a broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher every day, even indoors near windows and on cloudy days. Reapply every two to three hours when you are outdoors, and use a hat and shade where possible. Avoid deliberate tanning and sunbeds.</p>\n<p>If you are planning a holiday or prolonged sun exposure, tell us before your treatment so we can plan around it.</p>\n\n<h2>Treatment-specific notes</h2>\n<h3>After laser hair reduction</h3>\n<p>Expect mild redness and follicular bumps. Avoid heat, waxing, threading, and plucking. Shaving is usually fine between sessions. Use sunscreen on exposed areas. Learn more about <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>.</p>\n<h3>After pigmentation or facial rejuvenation treatments</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is essential. Follow the specific instructions for cleansing and actives. Do not pick at any flaking or crusting. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pigmentation-uneven-skin-tone/\">pigmentation treatment</a> and <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/facial-rejuvenation/\">facial rejuvenation</a>.</p>\n<h3>After acne treatments</h3>\n<p>Keep the routine gentle and avoid picking. If your skin is very dry or irritated, reduce the frequency of actives and contact us for advice. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/acne-acne-scars/\">acne and acne scar treatment</a>.</p>\n<h3>After injectable treatments</h3>\n<p>Follow the specific aftercare given at your appointment. Avoid rubbing or massaging the area unless instructed, and avoid strenuous exercise or heat for the period advised.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you experience any of the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Blistering or severe pain.</li>\n<li>Redness that is spreading or worsening after 48 hours.</li>\n<li>Fever, pus, or signs of infection.</li>\n<li>A reaction that worries you.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These problems are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly rather than treated at home.</p>\n\n<h2>A simple 7-day routine</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Morning:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser, broad-spectrum sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Evening:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser. Add a hydrating serum if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Throughout the week:</strong> no scrubs, no picking, no waxing, no new actives until your skin feels calm.</li>\n<li><strong>Before restarting actives:</strong> ask us or patch test on a small area.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If you are unsure whether something is normal, send us a message or book a follow-up. It is better to ask than to guess.</p>\n\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a> at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East. If this is your first visit, our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a> explains what to expect.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I wear make-up after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Follow the advice given at your appointment. Some treatments allow make-up the next day; others need a longer break. Keep it minimal and clean.</p>\n<h3>Can I exercise after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Avoid intense exercise, heat, and sweating for the period advised by your clinician, especially after laser or facial treatments.</p>\n<h3>Can I use vitamin C after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Wait until your skin is calm and your clinician confirms it is safe. Reintroduce one product at a time.</p>\n<h3>What if my skin feels dry?</h3>\n<p>Use a gentle moisturiser and a hydrating serum. Avoid scrubbing the flakes. If dryness is severe or painful, contact the clinic.</p>\n<h3>How long should I avoid the sun?</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is important every day, not just for a week. For treatments that affect pigmentation, strict protection during healing is essential.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Follow the aftercare instructions provided at your appointment, and contact the clinic if you have concerns.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Post-Treatment Skincare in Mira Road: A 7-Day Recovery Guide','A simple 7-day aftercare plan for laser and facial treatments: what to pause, what to use, and when to call the clinic in Mira Road East.','publish','closed','closed','','post-treatment-skincare-recovery-guide','','','2026-10-23 11:48:25','2026-10-23 11:48:25','',0,'http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/06/post-treatment-skincare-recovery-guide/',0,'post','',0),(78,1,'2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','<p>If you are tired of shaving, waxing, or threading on repeat, laser hair reduction can offer a longer-term answer. But the results depend on more than the machine: your skin and hair type, the clinic\'s assessment, the treatment plan, and how you care for your skin between sessions.</p>\n\n<p>This guide explains what a course of laser hair reduction at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East looks like, so you can arrive at your consultation with realistic expectations.</p>\n\n<h2>What is laser hair reduction?</h2>\n<p>Laser hair reduction uses concentrated light to target pigment in the hair follicle. The heat damages follicles that are in an active growth phase, which can reduce hair growth over a course of sessions. It is called <strong>reduction</strong> rather than permanent removal because hair growth cycles, hormones, and individual biology all affect how much hair returns.</p>\n<p>It can be used on the face, underarms, arms, legs, bikini line, back, and chest. Unlike waxing, it does not pull hair from the root; unlike shaving, it works below the skin\'s surface.</p>\n\n<h2>Is laser hair reduction right for you?</h2>\n<p>Laser works best on hair with plenty of pigment. Dark hair on light-to-medium skin is the classic combination, but modern devices and adjusted settings can treat a wider range of skin tones. Grey, white, and very light blonde hair usually responds poorly because there is little pigment for the laser to target.</p>\n<p>Your consultation will consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your skin tone, hair colour, and hair thickness.</li>\n<li>Hormonal factors such as PCOS, thyroid conditions, or sudden changes in hair growth.</li>\n<li>Medications and supplements that can increase light sensitivity.</li>\n<li>Pregnancy, active skin infections, recent sun exposure, or a history of keloid scarring.</li>\n<li>Previous waxing, threading, laser, or electrolysis.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If laser is not the right choice for you, we will say so and discuss alternatives.</p>\n\n<h2>Your consultation at Ma Lumière</h2>\n<p>The consultation is a medical assessment, not a quick sales conversation. We review your history, examine the treatment area, and discuss what you want to change. A patch test may be performed to see how your skin responds before a full session.</p>\n<p>You will leave with a clear plan: the areas to treat, an estimated number of sessions, spacing, aftercare, and the cost. If you are unsure what to expect from a first appointment, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens during a session</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Skin preparation.</strong> The area is cleaned and make-up or lotion is removed. We may shave the area if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Eye protection.</strong> You and the clinician wear protective eyewear.</li>\n<li><strong>Cooling and comfort.</strong> Cold air or a cooling gel helps protect the skin. Most people describe the pulses as a quick rubber-band snap.</li>\n<li><strong>Treatment.</strong> The clinician moves the handpiece over the area, adjusting settings to your skin and comfort. Most areas take between 20 and 60 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>After the session.</strong> Mild redness or small bumps are common and usually settle within a few hours.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>How many sessions will you need?</h2>\n<p>Hair grows in cycles, and only hair in the active growth phase responds to laser. That is why a single session is not enough. A typical plan is <strong>6 to 8 sessions, spaced 4 to 8 weeks apart</strong>, depending on the area and your hair growth.</p>\n<p>Hormonal areas such as the face, chin, and neck may need more sessions or occasional maintenance. Your plan will be reviewed as your hair growth changes.</p>\n<p>Between sessions, shaving is fine. Waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating are not, because they remove the hair root that the next session needs to target.</p>\n\n<h2>Aftercare that protects your results</h2>\n<p>For the first 24 to 48 hours, keep the area calm. Use a gentle cleanser and moisturiser, avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise if you tend to flush, and apply sunscreen every day. Pause retinoids, exfoliating acids, and scrubs until your clinician confirms it is safe to restart.</p>\n<p>Sun protection matters between sessions, especially on the face. If you are planning a holiday or extended sun exposure, tell us before booking so we can adjust the schedule.</p>\n<p>For a fuller aftercare plan, read our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/06/post-treatment-skincare-recovery-guide/\">7-day post-treatment skincare guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you develop blistering, severe pain, spreading redness, fever, or signs of infection. These are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly.</p>\n\n<h2>Why choose Ma Lumière in Mira Road East?</h2>\n<p>Laser results depend on assessment, settings, consistency, and aftercare. At Ma Lumière, treatments are planned and supervised with a medical approach, and we will tell you honestly if a different option is a better fit. Our clinic is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East.</p>\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction treatment</a>, browse the full <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Does laser hair reduction hurt?</h3>\n<p>Most people feel a quick snapping or warming sensation. Comfort depends on the area, your sensitivity, and the settings used. Cooling and adjusted settings help.</p>\n<h3>Can I shave between sessions?</h3>\n<p>Yes, shaving is usually allowed. Avoid waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating between sessions.</p>\n<h3>Is laser safe for darker skin?</h3>\n<p>It can be, but the device, settings, and clinician\'s experience matter. A consultation and patch test help determine whether treatment is appropriate for your skin.</p>\n<h3>How long do results last?</h3>\n<p>Many people enjoy long-lasting reduction, but hair can return over time, especially with hormonal changes. Maintenance sessions may help.</p>\n<h3>Can I have laser hair reduction in summer?</h3>\n<p>Yes, with careful sun protection and scheduling around sun exposure. Tell us about holidays, beach days, or prolonged outdoor time before treatment.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Suitability and results vary; a consultation is required to plan treatment for your skin and medical history.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Laser Hair Reduction in Mira Road: A Session-by-Session Guide','A clear, session-by-session guide to laser hair reduction in Mira Road — candidacy, comfort, aftercare, and how many sessions you may need.','inherit','closed','closed','','75-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','',75,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=78',0,'revision','',0),(79,1,'2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','<p>A skin consultation is where good treatment begins. It is not a sales pitch or a five-minute formality; it is the appointment where we work out what is happening in your skin, what you want to change, and which options are realistic for you.</p>\n<p>If you are booking your first appointment at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East, this guide explains what to expect and how to get the most from the conversation.</p>\n\n<h2>Why a consultation matters</h2>\n<p>Two people can have the same concern — acne, pigmentation, dullness, or hair thinning — for very different reasons. A treatment that suits one person may irritate another. The consultation connects the visible concern with your skin type, barrier health, medical history, lifestyle, and goals.</p>\n<p>It also gives you time to ask questions before committing to a plan. You should never feel rushed into a treatment.</p>\n\n<h2>What to bring</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Your current skincare.</strong> A list or photos of the products you use, including cleansers, actives, moisturisers, and sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Medications and supplements.</strong> Include prescription medicines, antibiotics, isotretinoin, hormonal treatments, and anything that can affect light sensitivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Allergies and past reactions.</strong> Tell us about reactions to products, lasers, peels, or anaesthetics.</li>\n<li><strong>Previous treatments.</strong> Dates and outcomes of facials, laser, peels, injectables, or dermatology treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos.</strong> If a concern comes and goes, bring photos of flare-ups.</li>\n<li><strong>Your goals and timeline.</strong> An event, a wedding, a holiday, or a gradual plan all change the approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Your questions.</strong> Write them down; it is easy to forget in the moment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What we assess</h2>\n<p>Every consultation starts with a conversation and a careful look at your skin. Depending on your concern, we may assess:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skin type, hydration, and barrier function.</li>\n<li>Acne, congestion, scarring, and pore size.</li>\n<li>Pigmentation, sun damage, and uneven tone.</li>\n<li>Texture, fine lines, and laxity.</li>\n<li>Hair growth, thinning, and scalp health.</li>\n<li>Lifestyle, sleep, stress, diet, and sun exposure.</li>\n<li>Medical and hormonal history that may affect the plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We will explain what we see in plain language and tell you whether the concern is best treated in clinic, at home, or with a combination of both.</p>\n\n<h2>How your treatment plan is built</h2>\n<p>A plan is more than a list of sessions. We consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>What matters most to you.</strong> Clearing acne, softening scarring, reducing hair, or improving glow are different goals.</li>\n<li><strong>What is realistic.</strong> Some concerns improve gradually; others need a staged approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Downtime.</strong> Work, events, and travel affect what we recommend.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance.</strong> Some treatments need follow-up to keep results.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget and pace.</strong> A plan should be sustainable, not a sprint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You will receive clear guidance on what to expect, how many sessions are estimated, what aftercare is needed, and what alternatives exist. If you are planning a wedding or a big event, our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pre-wedding-skin-preparation/\">pre-wedding skin preparation</a> page explains how we build a timeline around a date.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions worth asking</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What is causing my concern, and what would you rule out?</li>\n<li>What are my treatment options, including doing nothing for now?</li>\n<li>How many sessions might I need, and how will we review progress?</li>\n<li>What are the risks, side effects, and downtime?</li>\n<li>What should I pause or change in my routine before and after?</li>\n<li>What is the total cost, including follow-ups?</li>\n<li>What should I do if I do not see the result we expected?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is no such thing as a silly question. A good plan should make sense to you.</p>\n\n<h2>How to prepare</h2>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible, without heavy make-up, so we can assess it properly. Follow any instructions we send before your appointment. Do not start a new active ingredient or try a new facial right before the consultation; we want to see your skin as it normally behaves.</p>\n<p>If you are booking for laser hair reduction, avoid waxing or threading the area for a few weeks before your patch test. If you are booking for a skin concern, bring a list of products rather than the bottles.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens after the consultation</h2>\n<p>You will leave with a written plan and a clear next step. If a patch test is needed, we will arrange it. If you are ready to book, we will help you choose dates that fit your schedule and any events. If you want to think about it, that is fine too.</p>\n<p>Your plan can change. Skin changes, seasons change, and priorities change. We review progress as we go rather than locking you into a fixed package.</p>\n\n<h2>When to see a doctor sooner</h2>\n<p>Some concerns need prompt medical assessment rather than cosmetic treatment. Book sooner if you notice a new or changing mole, a sore that does not heal, bleeding, rapid hair loss, severe acne with pain or fever, or a rash that is spreading. These are not routine aesthetic concerns, and we will guide you to the right care.</p>\n\n<h2>Ready to book?</h2>\n<p>If you are looking for a <strong>skin consultation in Mira Road</strong>, Ma Lumière is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East. <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book your consultation</a>, explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or browse the <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/blog/\">skin journal</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How long does a consultation take?</h3>\n<p>Allow around 30 to 45 minutes, depending on your concern and the number of questions you have. A patch test may add a little time.</p>\n<h3>Do I need to prepare my skin?</h3>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible and bring a list of your current products. Follow any specific instructions sent before your appointment.</p>\n<h3>Will I be pressured to book a treatment?</h3>\n<p>No. The consultation is for assessment and planning. You can take time to decide.</p>\n<h3>Can I bring someone with me?</h3>\n<p>Yes, if it makes you more comfortable. Let us know in advance if you need extra time or support.</p>\n<h3>Do you treat men as well as women?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Skin and hair concerns are assessed individually, regardless of gender.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. A consultation is required to assess your skin and recommend treatment.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Your First Skin Consultation: What to Expect at Ma Lumière','What to bring, what we assess, and how your treatment plan is built at your first skin consultation in Mira Road East.','inherit','closed','closed','','76-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','',76,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=79',0,'revision','',0),(80,1,'2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','<p>The treatment is only part of the result. After a laser, facial, or skin treatment, your skin is temporarily more sensitive, and the right aftercare helps protect your results while reducing irritation.</p>\n<p>This guide covers the first week after treatment. Always follow the specific instructions given by your clinician, because aftercare depends on the treatment, your skin, and your medical history.</p>\n\n<h2>The first 24 hours</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Cleanse with a gentle, fragrance-free cleanser and lukewarm water. Avoid scrubbing.</li>\n<li>Apply a simple moisturiser and sunscreen. Skip make-up if your clinician advises it.</li>\n<li>Avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise that makes you flush.</li>\n<li>Do not use retinoids, exfoliating acids, scrubs, or strong active ingredients.</li>\n<li>Do not pick, scratch, or massage the treated area unless instructed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mild redness, warmth, or slight swelling can be normal. It should settle over hours to a couple of days.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 2 and 3</h2>\n<p>Keep the routine boring. Gentle cleanse, moisturise, and sunscreen. If your skin feels tight or dry, layer a hydrating serum under the moisturiser. Avoid exfoliation, waxing, threading, and hair removal creams on treated areas.</p>\n<p>If you had <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>, you may notice small bumps around the follicles. They usually settle. Do not scrub them. Shaving is generally fine unless your clinician has said otherwise.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 4 to 7</h2>\n<p>As redness settles, you can begin to return to your normal routine. Reintroduce one active ingredient at a time, every few days, rather than restarting everything at once. If your skin stings, flakes, or becomes red, stop and go back to the simple routine.</p>\n<p>Keep using sunscreen daily. Good sun protection is especially important after treatments for pigmentation, acne scarring, and facial rejuvenation.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients to pause</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Retinoids such as retinol, tretinoin, and adapalene.</li>\n<li>Exfoliating acids such as glycolic, salicylic, lactic, and mandelic acid.</li>\n<li>Physical scrubs, cleansing brushes, and at-home peeling devices.</li>\n<li>High-strength vitamin C, benzoyl peroxide, and alcohol-based toners if they sting.</li>\n<li>Fragrance-heavy products and essential oils on treated areas.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ask us when to restart each product. The timing depends on the treatment and how your skin is healing.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients that help</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ceramides</strong> to support the skin barrier.</li>\n<li><strong>Hyaluronic acid and glycerin</strong> for hydration.</li>\n<li><strong>Niacinamide</strong> if your skin tolerates it.</li>\n<li><strong>Panthenol and squalane</strong> for comfort.</li>\n<li><strong>Broad-spectrum sunscreen</strong> every morning.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do not need a ten-step routine. A gentle cleanser, a barrier-supporting moisturiser, and sunscreen are enough for most people in the first week.</p>\n\n<h2>Sun protection after treatment</h2>\n<p>Use a broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher every day, even indoors near windows and on cloudy days. Reapply every two to three hours when you are outdoors, and use a hat and shade where possible. Avoid deliberate tanning and sunbeds.</p>\n<p>If you are planning a holiday or prolonged sun exposure, tell us before your treatment so we can plan around it.</p>\n\n<h2>Treatment-specific notes</h2>\n<h3>After laser hair reduction</h3>\n<p>Expect mild redness and follicular bumps. Avoid heat, waxing, threading, and plucking. Shaving is usually fine between sessions. Use sunscreen on exposed areas. Learn more about <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>.</p>\n<h3>After pigmentation or facial rejuvenation treatments</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is essential. Follow the specific instructions for cleansing and actives. Do not pick at any flaking or crusting. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pigmentation-uneven-skin-tone/\">pigmentation treatment</a> and <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/facial-rejuvenation/\">facial rejuvenation</a>.</p>\n<h3>After acne treatments</h3>\n<p>Keep the routine gentle and avoid picking. If your skin is very dry or irritated, reduce the frequency of actives and contact us for advice. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/acne-acne-scars/\">acne and acne scar treatment</a>.</p>\n<h3>After injectable treatments</h3>\n<p>Follow the specific aftercare given at your appointment. Avoid rubbing or massaging the area unless instructed, and avoid strenuous exercise or heat for the period advised.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you notice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Blistering or severe pain.</li>\n<li>Redness that is spreading or worsening after 48 hours.</li>\n<li>Fever, pus, or signs of infection.</li>\n<li>A reaction that worries you.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These problems are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly rather than treated at home.</p>\n\n<h2>A simple 7-day routine</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Morning:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser, broad-spectrum sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Evening:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser. Add a hydrating serum if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Throughout the week:</strong> no scrubs, no picking, no waxing, no new actives until your skin feels calm.</li>\n<li><strong>Before restarting actives:</strong> ask us or patch test on a small area.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If you are unsure whether something is normal, send us a message or book a follow-up. It is better to ask than to guess.</p>\n\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a> at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East. If this is your first visit, our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a> explains what to expect.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I wear make-up after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Follow the advice given at your appointment. Some treatments allow make-up the next day; others need a longer break. Keep it minimal and clean.</p>\n<h3>Can I exercise after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Avoid intense exercise, heat, and sweating for the period advised by your clinician, especially after laser or facial treatments.</p>\n<h3>Can I use vitamin C after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Wait until your skin is calm and your clinician confirms it is safe. Reintroduce one product at a time.</p>\n<h3>What if my skin feels dry?</h3>\n<p>Use a gentle moisturiser and a hydrating serum. Avoid scrubbing the flakes. If dryness is severe or painful, contact the clinic.</p>\n<h3>How long should I avoid the sun?</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is important every day, not just for a week. For treatments that affect pigmentation, strict protection during healing is essential.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Follow the aftercare instructions provided at your appointment, and contact the clinic if you have concerns.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Post-Treatment Skincare: A 7-Day Recovery Guide','A simple 7-day aftercare plan for laser and facial treatments: what to pause, what to use, and when to call the clinic.','inherit','closed','closed','','77-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','',77,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=80',0,'revision','',0),(81,1,'2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','At Ma Lumière, dermatology is a conversation. We begin every journey by listening — then build a plan around your skin, your concerns and your goals. This journal will grow with clinic-approved guidance on skin health, treatments and care.\n\n[CLINIC JOURNAL CONTENT REQUIRED]','Welcome to Ma Lumière','A note on how we work at the clinic.','inherit','closed','closed','','13-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:12:53','2026-10-23 11:12:53','',13,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=81',0,'revision','',0),(82,1,'2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','<p>If you are tired of shaving, waxing, or threading on repeat, laser hair reduction can offer a longer-term answer. But the results depend on more than the machine: your skin and hair type, the clinic\'s assessment, the treatment plan, and how you care for your skin between sessions.</p>\n\n<p>This guide explains what a course of laser hair reduction at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East looks like, so you can arrive at your consultation with realistic expectations.</p>\n\n<h2>What is laser hair reduction?</h2>\n<p>Laser hair reduction uses concentrated light to target pigment in the hair follicle. The heat damages follicles that are in an active growth phase, which can reduce hair growth over a course of sessions. It is called <strong>reduction</strong> rather than permanent removal because hair growth cycles, hormones, and individual biology all affect how much hair returns.</p>\n<p>It can be used on the face, underarms, arms, legs, bikini line, back, and chest. Unlike waxing, it does not pull hair from the root; unlike shaving, it works below the skin\'s surface.</p>\n\n<h2>Is laser hair reduction right for you?</h2>\n<p>Laser works best on hair with plenty of pigment. Dark hair on light-to-medium skin is the classic combination, but modern devices and adjusted settings can treat a wider range of skin tones. Grey, white, and very light blonde hair usually responds poorly because there is little pigment for the laser to target.</p>\n<p>Your consultation will consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your skin tone, hair colour, and hair thickness.</li>\n<li>Hormonal factors such as PCOS, thyroid conditions, or sudden changes in hair growth.</li>\n<li>Medications and supplements that can increase light sensitivity.</li>\n<li>Pregnancy, active skin infections, recent sun exposure, or a history of keloid scarring.</li>\n<li>Previous waxing, threading, laser, or electrolysis.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If laser is not the right choice for you, we will say so and discuss alternatives.</p>\n\n<h2>Your consultation at Ma Lumière</h2>\n<p>The consultation is a medical assessment, not a quick sales conversation. We review your history, examine the treatment area, and discuss what you want to change. A patch test may be performed to see how your skin responds before a full session.</p>\n<p>You will leave with a clear plan: the areas to treat, an estimated number of sessions, spacing, aftercare, and the cost. If you are unsure what to expect from a first appointment, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens during a session</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Skin preparation.</strong> The area is cleaned and make-up or lotion is removed. We may shave the area if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Eye protection.</strong> You and the clinician wear protective eyewear.</li>\n<li><strong>Cooling and comfort.</strong> Cold air or a cooling gel helps protect the skin. Most people describe the pulses as a quick rubber-band snap.</li>\n<li><strong>Treatment.</strong> The clinician moves the handpiece over the area, adjusting settings to your skin and comfort. Most areas take between 20 and 60 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>After the session.</strong> Mild redness or small bumps are common and usually settle within a few hours.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>How many sessions will you need?</h2>\n<p>Hair grows in cycles, and only hair in the active growth phase responds to laser. That is why a single session is not enough. A typical plan is <strong>6 to 8 sessions, spaced 4 to 8 weeks apart</strong>, depending on the area and your hair growth.</p>\n<p>Hormonal areas such as the face, chin, and neck may need more sessions or occasional maintenance. Your plan will be reviewed as your hair growth changes.</p>\n<p>Between sessions, shaving is fine. Waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating are not, because they remove the hair root that the next session needs to target.</p>\n\n<h2>Aftercare that protects your results</h2>\n<p>For the first 24 to 48 hours, keep the area calm. Use a gentle cleanser and moisturiser, avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise if you tend to flush, and apply sunscreen every day. Pause retinoids, exfoliating acids, and scrubs until your clinician confirms it is safe to restart.</p>\n<p>Sun protection matters between sessions, especially on the face. If you are planning a holiday or extended sun exposure, tell us before booking so we can adjust the schedule.</p>\n<p>For a fuller aftercare plan, read our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/06/post-treatment-skincare-recovery-guide/\">7-day post-treatment skincare guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you develop blistering, severe pain, spreading redness, fever, or signs of infection. These are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly.</p>\n\n<h2>Why choose Ma Lumière in Mira Road East?</h2>\n<p>Laser results depend on assessment, settings, consistency, and aftercare. At Ma Lumière, treatments are planned and supervised with a medical approach, and we will tell you honestly if a different option is a better fit. Our clinic is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East.</p>\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction treatment</a>, browse the full <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Does laser hair reduction hurt?</h3>\n<p>Most people feel a quick snapping or warming sensation. Comfort depends on the area, your sensitivity, and the settings used. Cooling and adjusted settings help.</p>\n<h3>Can I shave between sessions?</h3>\n<p>Yes, shaving is usually allowed. Avoid waxing, threading, plucking, and epilating between sessions.</p>\n<h3>Is laser safe for darker skin?</h3>\n<p>It can be, but the device, settings, and clinician\'s experience matter. A consultation and patch test help determine whether treatment is appropriate for your skin.</p>\n<h3>How long do results last?</h3>\n<p>Many people enjoy long-lasting reduction, but hair can return over time, especially with hormonal changes. Maintenance sessions may help.</p>\n<h3>Can I have laser hair reduction in summer?</h3>\n<p>Yes, with careful sun protection and scheduling around sun exposure. Tell us about holidays, beach days, or prolonged outdoor time before treatment.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Suitability and results vary; a consultation is required to plan treatment for your skin and medical history.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Laser Hair Reduction in Mira Road: A Session-by-Session Guide','A clear, session-by-session guide to laser hair reduction in Mira Road East — candidacy, comfort, aftercare, and how many sessions you may need.','inherit','closed','closed','','75-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','',75,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=82',0,'revision','',0),(83,1,'2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','<p>A skin consultation is where good treatment begins. It is not a sales pitch or a five-minute formality; it is the appointment where we work out what is happening in your skin, what you want to change, and which options are realistic for you.</p>\n<p>If you are booking your first appointment at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East, this guide explains what to expect and how to get the most from the conversation.</p>\n\n<h2>Why a consultation matters</h2>\n<p>Two people can have the same concern — acne, pigmentation, dullness, or hair thinning — for very different reasons. A treatment that suits one person may irritate another. The consultation connects the visible concern with your skin type, barrier health, medical history, lifestyle, and goals.</p>\n<p>It also gives you time to ask questions before committing to a plan. You should never feel rushed into a treatment.</p>\n\n<h2>What to bring</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Your current skincare.</strong> A list or photos of the products you use, including cleansers, actives, moisturisers, and sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Medications and supplements.</strong> Include prescription medicines, antibiotics, isotretinoin, hormonal treatments, and anything that can affect light sensitivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Allergies and past reactions.</strong> Tell us about reactions to products, lasers, peels, or anaesthetics.</li>\n<li><strong>Previous treatments.</strong> Dates and outcomes of facials, laser, peels, injectables, or dermatology treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos.</strong> If a concern comes and goes, bring photos of flare-ups.</li>\n<li><strong>Your goals and timeline.</strong> An event, a wedding, a holiday, or a gradual plan all change the approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Your questions.</strong> Write them down; it is easy to forget in the moment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What we assess</h2>\n<p>Every consultation starts with a conversation and a careful look at your skin. Depending on your concern, we may assess:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skin type, hydration, and barrier function.</li>\n<li>Acne, congestion, scarring, and pore size.</li>\n<li>Pigmentation, sun damage, and uneven tone.</li>\n<li>Texture, fine lines, and laxity.</li>\n<li>Hair growth, thinning, and scalp health.</li>\n<li>Lifestyle, sleep, stress, diet, and sun exposure.</li>\n<li>Medical and hormonal history that may affect the plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We will explain what we see in plain language and tell you whether the concern is best treated in clinic, at home, or with a combination of both.</p>\n\n<h2>How your treatment plan is built</h2>\n<p>A plan is more than a list of sessions. We consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>What matters most to you.</strong> Clearing acne, softening scarring, reducing hair, or improving glow are different goals.</li>\n<li><strong>What is realistic.</strong> Some concerns improve gradually; others need a staged approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Downtime.</strong> Work, events, and travel affect what we recommend.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance.</strong> Some treatments need follow-up to keep results.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget and pace.</strong> A plan should be sustainable, not a sprint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You will receive clear guidance on what to expect, how many sessions are estimated, what aftercare is needed, and what alternatives exist. If you are planning a wedding or a big event, our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pre-wedding-skin-preparation/\">pre-wedding skin preparation</a> page explains how we build a timeline around a date.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions worth asking</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What is causing my concern, and what would you rule out?</li>\n<li>What are my treatment options, including doing nothing for now?</li>\n<li>How many sessions might I need, and how will we review progress?</li>\n<li>What are the risks, side effects, and downtime?</li>\n<li>What should I pause or change in my routine before and after?</li>\n<li>What is the total cost, including follow-ups?</li>\n<li>What should I do if I do not see the result we expected?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is no such thing as a silly question. A good plan should make sense to you.</p>\n\n<h2>How to prepare</h2>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible, without heavy make-up, so we can assess it properly. Follow any instructions we send before your appointment. Do not start a new active ingredient or try a new facial right before the consultation; we want to see your skin as it normally behaves.</p>\n<p>If you are booking for laser hair reduction, avoid waxing or threading the area for a few weeks before your patch test. If you are booking for a skin concern, bring a list of products rather than the bottles.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens after the consultation</h2>\n<p>You will leave with a written plan and a clear next step. If a patch test is needed, we will arrange it. If you are ready to book, we will help you choose dates that fit your schedule and any events. If you want to think about it, that is fine too.</p>\n<p>Your plan can change. Skin changes, seasons change, and priorities change. We review progress as we go rather than locking you into a fixed package.</p>\n\n<h2>When to see a doctor sooner</h2>\n<p>Some concerns need prompt medical assessment rather than cosmetic treatment. Book sooner if you notice a new or changing mole, a sore that does not heal, bleeding, rapid hair loss, severe acne with pain or fever, or a rash that is spreading. These are not routine aesthetic concerns, and we will guide you to the right care.</p>\n\n<h2>Ready to book?</h2>\n<p>If you are looking for a <strong>skin consultation in Mira Road</strong>, Ma Lumière is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East. <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book your consultation</a>, explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or browse the <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/blog/\">skin journal</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How long does a consultation take?</h3>\n<p>Allow around 30 to 45 minutes, depending on your concern and the number of questions you have. A patch test may add a little time.</p>\n<h3>Do I need to prepare my skin?</h3>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible and bring a list of your current products. Follow any specific instructions sent before your appointment.</p>\n<h3>Will I be pressured to book a treatment?</h3>\n<p>No. The consultation is for assessment and planning. You can take time to decide.</p>\n<h3>Can I bring someone with me?</h3>\n<p>Yes, if it makes you more comfortable. Let us know in advance if you need extra time or support.</p>\n<h3>Do you treat men as well as women?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Skin and hair concerns are assessed individually, regardless of gender.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. A consultation is required to assess your skin and recommend treatment.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Your First Skin Consultation: What to Expect at Ma Lumière','What to bring, what we assess, and how your treatment plan is built at your first skin consultation in Mira Road East — plus questions worth asking.','inherit','closed','closed','','76-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','',76,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=83',0,'revision','',0),(84,1,'2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','<p>The treatment is only part of the result. After a laser, facial, or skin treatment, your skin is temporarily more sensitive, and the right aftercare helps protect your results while reducing irritation.</p>\n<p>This guide covers the first week after treatment. Always follow the specific instructions given by your clinician, because aftercare depends on the treatment, your skin, and your medical history.</p>\n\n<h2>The first 24 hours</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Cleanse with a gentle, fragrance-free cleanser and lukewarm water. Avoid scrubbing.</li>\n<li>Apply a simple moisturiser and sunscreen. Skip make-up if your clinician advises it.</li>\n<li>Avoid hot showers, saunas, steam rooms, and intense exercise that makes you flush.</li>\n<li>Do not use retinoids, exfoliating acids, scrubs, or strong active ingredients.</li>\n<li>Do not pick, scratch, or massage the treated area unless instructed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mild redness, warmth, or slight swelling can be normal. It should settle over hours to a couple of days.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 2 and 3</h2>\n<p>Keep the routine boring. Gentle cleanse, moisturise, and sunscreen. If your skin feels tight or dry, layer a hydrating serum under the moisturiser. Avoid exfoliation, waxing, threading, and hair removal creams on treated areas.</p>\n<p>If you had <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>, you may notice small bumps around the follicles. They usually settle. Do not scrub them. Shaving is generally fine unless your clinician has said otherwise.</p>\n\n<h2>Days 4 to 7</h2>\n<p>As redness settles, you can begin to return to your normal routine. Reintroduce one active ingredient at a time, every few days, rather than restarting everything at once. If your skin stings, flakes, or becomes red, stop and go back to the simple routine.</p>\n<p>Keep using sunscreen daily. Good sun protection is especially important after treatments for pigmentation, acne scarring, and facial rejuvenation.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients to pause</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Retinoids such as retinol, tretinoin, and adapalene.</li>\n<li>Exfoliating acids such as glycolic, salicylic, lactic, and mandelic acid.</li>\n<li>Physical scrubs, cleansing brushes, and at-home peeling devices.</li>\n<li>High-strength vitamin C, benzoyl peroxide, and alcohol-based toners if they sting.</li>\n<li>Fragrance-heavy products and essential oils on treated areas.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ask us when to restart each product. The timing depends on the treatment and how your skin is healing.</p>\n\n<h2>Ingredients that help</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ceramides</strong> to support the skin barrier.</li>\n<li><strong>Hyaluronic acid and glycerin</strong> for hydration.</li>\n<li><strong>Niacinamide</strong> if your skin tolerates it.</li>\n<li><strong>Panthenol and squalane</strong> for comfort.</li>\n<li><strong>Broad-spectrum sunscreen</strong> every morning.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do not need a ten-step routine. A gentle cleanser, a barrier-supporting moisturiser, and sunscreen are enough for most people in the first week.</p>\n\n<h2>Sun protection after treatment</h2>\n<p>Use a broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher every day, even indoors near windows and on cloudy days. Reapply every two to three hours when you are outdoors, and use a hat and shade where possible. Avoid deliberate tanning and sunbeds.</p>\n<p>If you are planning a holiday or prolonged sun exposure, tell us before your treatment so we can plan around it.</p>\n\n<h2>Treatment-specific notes</h2>\n<h3>After laser hair reduction</h3>\n<p>Expect mild redness and follicular bumps. Avoid heat, waxing, threading, and plucking. Shaving is usually fine between sessions. Use sunscreen on exposed areas. Learn more about <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/laser-hair-reduction/\">laser hair reduction</a>.</p>\n<h3>After pigmentation or facial rejuvenation treatments</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is essential. Follow the specific instructions for cleansing and actives. Do not pick at any flaking or crusting. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pigmentation-uneven-skin-tone/\">pigmentation treatment</a> and <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/facial-rejuvenation/\">facial rejuvenation</a>.</p>\n<h3>After acne treatments</h3>\n<p>Keep the routine gentle and avoid picking. If your skin is very dry or irritated, reduce the frequency of actives and contact us for advice. Explore <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/acne-acne-scars/\">acne and acne scar treatment</a>.</p>\n<h3>After injectable treatments</h3>\n<p>Follow the specific aftercare given at your appointment. Avoid rubbing or massaging the area unless instructed, and avoid strenuous exercise or heat for the period advised.</p>\n\n<h2>When to call the clinic</h2>\n<p>Contact us if you notice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Blistering or severe pain.</li>\n<li>Redness that is spreading or worsening after 48 hours.</li>\n<li>Fever, pus, or signs of infection.</li>\n<li>A reaction that worries you.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These problems are uncommon, but they should be assessed promptly rather than treated at home.</p>\n\n<h2>A simple 7-day routine</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Morning:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser, broad-spectrum sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Evening:</strong> gentle cleanser, moisturiser. Add a hydrating serum if needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Throughout the week:</strong> no scrubs, no picking, no waxing, no new actives until your skin feels calm.</li>\n<li><strong>Before restarting actives:</strong> ask us or patch test on a small area.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If you are unsure whether something is normal, send us a message or book a follow-up. It is better to ask than to guess.</p>\n\n<p>Explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">book a consultation</a> at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East. If this is your first visit, our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/13/first-skin-consultation-mira-road/\">your first skin consultation</a> explains what to expect.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I wear make-up after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Follow the advice given at your appointment. Some treatments allow make-up the next day; others need a longer break. Keep it minimal and clean.</p>\n<h3>Can I exercise after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Avoid intense exercise, heat, and sweating for the period advised by your clinician, especially after laser or facial treatments.</p>\n<h3>Can I use vitamin C after a treatment?</h3>\n<p>Wait until your skin is calm and your clinician confirms it is safe. Reintroduce one product at a time.</p>\n<h3>What if my skin feels dry?</h3>\n<p>Use a gentle moisturiser and a hydrating serum. Avoid scrubbing the flakes. If dryness is severe or painful, contact the clinic.</p>\n<h3>How long should I avoid the sun?</h3>\n<p>Sun protection is important every day, not just for a week. For treatments that affect pigmentation, strict protection during healing is essential.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. Follow the aftercare instructions provided at your appointment, and contact the clinic if you have concerns.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Post-Treatment Skincare: A 7-Day Recovery Guide','A simple 7-day aftercare plan for laser and facial treatments: what to pause, what to use, and when to call the clinic in Mira Road East.','inherit','closed','closed','','77-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:17:38','2026-10-23 11:17:38','',77,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=84',0,'revision','',0),(85,1,'2026-10-23 11:28:50','2026-10-23 11:28:50','<p>A skin consultation is where good treatment begins. It is not a sales pitch or a five-minute formality; it is the appointment where we work out what is happening in your skin, what you want to change, and which options are realistic for you.</p>\n<p>If you are booking your first appointment at Ma Lumière in Mira Road East, this guide explains what to expect and how to get the most from the conversation.</p>\n\n<h2>Why a consultation matters</h2>\n<p>Two people can have the same concern — acne, pigmentation, dullness, or hair thinning — for very different reasons. A treatment that suits one person may irritate another. The consultation connects the visible concern with your skin type, barrier health, medical history, lifestyle, and goals.</p>\n<p>It also gives you time to ask questions before committing to a plan. You should never feel rushed into a treatment.</p>\n\n<h2>What to bring</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Your current skincare.</strong> A list or photos of the products you use, including cleansers, actives, moisturisers, and sunscreen.</li>\n<li><strong>Medications and supplements.</strong> Include prescription medicines, antibiotics, isotretinoin, hormonal treatments, and anything that can affect light sensitivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Allergies and past reactions.</strong> Tell us about reactions to products, lasers, peels, or anaesthetics.</li>\n<li><strong>Previous treatments.</strong> Dates and outcomes of facials, laser, peels, injectables, or dermatology treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos.</strong> If a concern comes and goes, bring photos of flare-ups.</li>\n<li><strong>Your goals and timeline.</strong> An event, a wedding, a holiday, or a gradual plan all change the approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Your questions.</strong> Write them down; it is easy to forget in the moment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What we assess</h2>\n<p>Every consultation starts with a conversation and a careful look at your skin. Depending on your concern, we may assess:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skin type, hydration, and barrier function.</li>\n<li>Acne, congestion, scarring, and pore size.</li>\n<li>Pigmentation, sun damage, and uneven tone.</li>\n<li>Texture, fine lines, and laxity.</li>\n<li>Hair growth, thinning, and scalp health.</li>\n<li>Lifestyle, sleep, stress, diet, and sun exposure.</li>\n<li>Medical and hormonal history that may affect the plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We will explain what we see in plain language and tell you whether the concern is best treated in clinic, at home, or with a combination of both.</p>\n\n<h2>How your treatment plan is built</h2>\n<p>A plan is more than a list of sessions. We consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>What matters most to you.</strong> Clearing acne, softening scarring, reducing hair, or improving glow are different goals.</li>\n<li><strong>What is realistic.</strong> Some concerns improve gradually; others need a staged approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Downtime.</strong> Work, events, and travel affect what we recommend.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance.</strong> Some treatments need follow-up to keep results.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget and pace.</strong> A plan should be sustainable, not a sprint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You will receive clear guidance on what to expect, how many sessions are estimated, what aftercare is needed, and what alternatives exist. If you are planning a wedding or a big event, our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatment/pre-wedding-skin-preparation/\">pre-wedding skin preparation</a> page explains how we build a timeline around a date.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions worth asking</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What is causing my concern, and what would you rule out?</li>\n<li>What are my treatment options, including doing nothing for now?</li>\n<li>How many sessions might I need, and how will we review progress?</li>\n<li>What are the risks, side effects, and downtime?</li>\n<li>What should I pause or change in my routine before and after?</li>\n<li>What is the total cost, including follow-ups?</li>\n<li>What should I do if I do not see the result we expected?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is no such thing as a silly question. A good plan should make sense to you.</p>\n\n<h2>How to prepare</h2>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible, without heavy make-up, so we can assess it properly. Follow any instructions we send before your appointment. Do not start a new active ingredient or try a new facial right before the consultation; we want to see your skin as it normally behaves.</p>\n<p>If you are booking for laser hair reduction, avoid waxing or threading the area for a few weeks before your patch test. If you are booking for a skin concern, bring a list of products rather than the bottles.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens after the consultation</h2>\n<p>You will leave with a written plan and a clear next step. If a patch test is needed, we will arrange it. If you are ready to book, we will help you choose dates that fit your schedule and any events. If you want to think about it, that is fine too.</p>\n<p>Your plan can change. Skin changes, seasons change, and priorities change. We review progress as we go rather than locking you into a fixed package.</p>\n\n<h2>When to see a doctor sooner</h2>\n<p>Some concerns need prompt medical assessment rather than cosmetic treatment. Book sooner if you notice a new or changing mole, a sore that does not heal, bleeding, rapid hair loss, severe acne with pain or fever, or a rash that is spreading. These are not routine aesthetic concerns, and we will guide you to the right care.</p>\n\n<h2>Ready to book?</h2>\n<p>If you are looking for a <strong>skin consultation in Mira Road</strong>, Ma Lumière is located at Vasudev Sky High, Kanakia Road, Beverly Park, Mira Road East. <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book your consultation</a>, explore our <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/treatments/\">treatment menu</a>, read our guide to <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/2026/10/20/laser-hair-reduction-mira-road-guide/\">laser hair reduction</a>, or browse the <a href=\"http://localhost/malumere/blog/\">skin journal</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How long does a consultation take?</h3>\n<p>Allow around 30 to 45 minutes, depending on your concern and the number of questions you have. A patch test may add a little time.</p>\n<h3>Do I need to prepare my skin?</h3>\n<p>Come with clean skin if possible and bring a list of your current products. Follow any specific instructions sent before your appointment.</p>\n<h3>Will I be pressured to book a treatment?</h3>\n<p>No. The consultation is for assessment and planning. You can take time to decide.</p>\n<h3>Can I bring someone with me?</h3>\n<p>Yes, if it makes you more comfortable. Let us know in advance if you need extra time or support.</p>\n<h3>Can I book a consultation if I am not sure what treatment I need?</h3>\n<p>Yes. The consultation is designed to narrow down the options. You do not need to choose a treatment before you arrive.</p>\n\n<p><em>This article is general information, not medical advice. A consultation is required to assess your skin and recommend treatment.</em></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"btn btn--primary\" href=\"http://localhost/malumere/book-consultation/\">Book a consultation</a></p>','Your First Skin Consultation: What to Expect at Ma Lumière','What to bring, what we assess, and how your treatment plan is built at your first skin consultation in Mira Road East — plus questions worth asking.','inherit','closed','closed','','76-revision-v1','','','2026-10-23 11:28:50','2026-10-23 11:28:50','',76,'http://localhost/malumere/?p=85',0,'revision','',0),(86,1,'2026-10-23 11:29:34','2026-10-23 11:29:34','<p>A skin consultation is where good treatment begins. It is not a sales pitch or a five-minute formality; it is the appointment where we work out what is happening in your skin, what you want to change, and which options are realistic